{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DiTDLvMYyamdY7naZxfXny","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Median档核心叙事：SOPBench部分复制C1（Δ~20pp, OR~3.5, 显著但远弱于τ²-bench的34pp），\n2\t  确认binary effect跨domain成立但effect size显著依赖benchmark strictness。 类型排序部分对齐（ρ~0.5）：incompleteness仍high-risk，但auth_scope在SOPBench\n3\t  因healthcare domain的strict protocol culture排序大幅下降（从#2→#4）， lexical在bank domain因术语歧义上升。C1\n4\t  claim加domain-dependence caveat （''effect size varies by benchmark strictness and\n5\t  domain''）。 C2从''universal 3-tier hierarchy''降为''robust in customer-service, partially\n6\t  replicated in healthcare/banking''。C3因within-judge fragility + SOPBench不支持进一步降为\n7\t  appendix exploratory。C4 interaction保持但soften为''domain-robust for extreme types,\n8\t  domain-sensitive for mid-tier''。SOPBench放appendix，main text一句话总结。 一位审稿人对V=0.137\n9\t  practical significance要求3-tier TOST justification， 一位审稿人对C3 fragility要求softening。Paper从''universal\n10\t  law''退为 ''robust phenomenon with domain moderation''。预期ARR avg 3.0-3.5。 plan_013的7-model\n11\t  replication（含Gemini/LLaMA）补偿SOPBench弱复制， 形成''binary effect universally replicates,\n12\t  severity ordering is domain-moderated''的平衡叙事。\n13\t\n14\t  '\n15\timagined_experiments:\n16\t- name: full_study_clause_generation\n17\t  plan_id: plan_001\n18\t  description: '生成剩余140条clause pairs，达到300条（50/type × 6 types）。 验证跨类型平衡、CP混合格式、质量一致性。\n19\t\n20\t    '\n21\t  expected_results:\n22\t    total_clauses_generated: 300\n23\t    new_clauses: 140\n24\t    per_type_count: 50\n25\t    format_mix_cp_labeled_pct: 0.6\n26\t    format_mix_cp_unlabeled_pct: 0.4\n27\t    avg_token_delta_spec_layer: 34.0\n28\t    avg_token_delta_ling_layer: 14.8\n29\t    quality_review_pass_rate: 0.92\n30\t    clauses_requiring_revision: 11\n31\t  result_rationale: 'Clause generation是确定性工作，median档不影响此步结果。300条全部完成。 Spec/ling token\n32\t    delta不对称（spec ~34 vs ling ~15 tokens）在后续analysis中 被logistic regression控制（token_delta作为covariate），但reviewer会在RC7中\n33\t    追问incompleteness的information asymmetry。~8%需revision，集中在auth_scope （permission\n34\t    boundary的\"足够模糊但不过度\"平衡）和incompleteness （minimal information addition约束）。CP混合格式60/40\n35\t    labeled/unlabeled 按reviewer建议执行。\n36\t\n37\t    '\n38\t  tables:\n39\t  - name: Clause Generation Summary\n40\t    columns:\n41\t    - type\n42\t    - layer\n43\t    - n_pairs\n44\t    - avg_token_delta\n45\t    - revision_needed\n46\t    rows:\n47\t    - - authorization_scope\n48\t      - spec\n49\t      - 50\n50\t      - 36.1\n51\t      - 3\n52\t    - - conditional_precedence\n53\t      - spec\n54\t      - 50\n55\t      - 31.4\n56\t      - 1\n57\t    - - incompleteness\n58\t      - spec\n59\t      - 50\n60\t      - 34.6\n61\t      - 4\n62\t    - - lexical\n63\t      - ling\n64\t      - 50\n65\t      - 18.2\n66\t      - 2\n67\t    - - coreferential\n68\t      - ling\n69\t      - 50\n70\t      - 7.8\n71\t      - 1\n72\t    - - scopal\n73\t      - ling\n74\t      - 50\n75\t      - 18.3\n76\t      - 0\n77\t  figures_description:\n78\t  - Token delta distribution boxplot per type, showing spec-layer types consistently\n79\t    higher (mean 34.0 vs 14.8)\n80\t  analysis: 'Clause generation成功。spec-layer token delta显著高于ling-layer（t-test p<0.001），\n81\t    结构性差异——消除spec-layer模糊需要更多tokens。plan_004中token_delta作covariate控制。 此步骤不受median档位影响，所有downstream不确定性来自execution和SOPBench\n82\t    replication。\n83\t\n84\t    '\n85\t- name: new_type_mini_pilot\n86\t  plan_id: plan_001b\n87\t  description: 'Coreferential和authorization_scope的mini-pilot验证。 5 clauses/type × 2\n88\t    conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes。\n89\t\n90\t    '\n91\t  expected_results:\n92\t    total_episodes: 20\n93\t    auth_scope_amb_violation_rate: 0.6\n94\t    auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.1\n95\t    coref_amb_violation_rate: 0.2\n96\t    coref_unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n97\t    systematic_issues_found: 1\n98\t    issue_description: 2/5 auth_scope unambiguous clauses含residual boundary ambiguity需revision\n99\t  result_rationale: 'Mini-pilot在median档下发现auth_scope的unambiguous baseline偏高（10%，在<15%阈值内但不理想），\n100\t    因2条unambiguous clause的permission boundary仍有subtle残余模糊。 这是expected的clause quality\n101\t    iteration——auth_scope本身定义\"清晰边界\"就比其他类型更难。 Coreferential表现正常（amb 20%低于其他类型，unamb\n102\t    0%干净）， 验证coreferential作为low-tier的定位。revision后不阻塞full study。 N=20 power极低，仅作sanity\n103\t    check用。\n104\t\n105\t    '\n106\t  tables:\n107\t  - name: Mini-pilot Results\n108\t    columns:\n109\t    - type\n110\t    - condition\n111\t    - n\n112\t    - violation_rate\n113\t    - pass\n114\t    rows:\n115\t    - - auth_scope\n116\t      - ambiguous\n117\t      - 5\n118\t      - 3/5 (60%)\n119\t      - 'yes'\n120\t    - - auth_scope\n121\t      - unambiguous\n122\t      - 5\n123\t      - 0.5/5 (10%)\n124\t      - yes (marginal)\n125\t    - - coreferential\n126\t      - ambiguous\n127\t      - 5\n128\t      - 1/5 (20%)\n129\t      - 'yes'\n130\t    - - coreferential\n131\t      - unambiguous\n132\t      - 5\n133\t      - 0/5 (0%)\n134\t      - 'yes'\n135\t  figures_description: []\n136\t  analysis: 'Mini-pilot通过。Auth_scope unambiguous baseline 10%提示需收紧permission boundary定义。\n137\t    修复2条clause后进入full study。\n138\t\n139\t    '\n140\t- name: full_study_api\n141\t  plan_id: plan_002\n142\t  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6)\n143\t    = 1,800 episodes。 Cross-judge evaluation。\n144\t\n145\t    '\n146\t  expected_results:\n147\t    total_episodes: 1800\n148\t    episodes_valid: 1793\n149\t    episodes_failed: 7\n150\t    overall_amb_violation_rate: 0.387\n151\t    overall_unamb_violation_rate: 0.055\n152\t    overall_delta_pp: 33.2\n153\t    gpt54_amb_rate: 0.41\n154\t    gpt54_unamb_rate: 0.05\n155\t    gpt54_delta_pp: 36.0\n156\t    gpt41_amb_rate: 0.4\n157\t    gpt41_unamb_rate: 0.057\n158\t    gpt41_delta_pp: 34.3\n159\t    claude_amb_rate: 0.3\n160\t    claude_unamb_rate: 0.047\n161\t    claude_delta_pp: 25.3\n162\t    cross_judge_agreement_kappa: 0.87\n163\t    api_cost_usd: 340\n164\t    runtime_hours: 18\n165\t  result_rationale: 'Median档下API models结果与prior 5-model data高度一致 （实际completed: gpt-5.4\n166\t    Δ38.3pp, gpt-4.1 Δ34.7pp, claude Δ25.7pp）。 300 clauses的full coverage相比pilot更完整，但增加了harder\n167\t    edge cases， 使overall delta从prior的34.0pp略降至~33.2pp。Claude的delta ~25pp 确认其作为most-robust\n168\t    model的地位。Cross-judge κ=0.87表面良好， 但median档的关键转折在plan_009：LLM-LLM agreement掩盖了共享的\n169\t    systematic over-classification bias。7个failed episodes源于API timeout/ τ²-bench环境偶发错误，不影响统计力。\n170\t\n171\t    '\n172\t  tables:\n173\t  - name: Per-model Summary (API models)\n174\t    columns:\n175\t    - model\n176\t    - n_episodes\n177\t    - amb_rate\n178\t    - unamb_rate\n179\t    - delta_pp\n180\t    - mcnemar_p\n181\t    rows:\n182\t    - - gpt-5.4\n183\t      - 600\n184\t      - 0.41\n185\t      - 0.05\n186\t      - 36.0\n187\t      - <1e-20\n188\t    - - gpt-4.1\n189\t      - 600\n190\t      - 0.4\n191\t      - 0.057\n192\t      - 34.3\n193\t      - <1e-18\n194\t    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n195\t      - 600\n196\t      - 0.3\n197\t      - 0.047\n198\t      - 25.3\n199\t      - <1e-14\n200\t  figures_description:\n201\t  - 'Per-model paired bar chart: ambiguous vs unambiguous violation rates with 95%\n202\t    CI error bars'\n203\t  analysis: '三个API模型全部显示massive binary effect。Claude最robust，GPT-5.4最vulnerable。 这些raw\n204\t    numbers在plan_009 judge calibration后会被corrected， 但qualitative pattern（Claude <<\n205\t    GPT models）不会改变。\n206\t\n207\t    '\n208\t- name: full_study_opensource\n209\t  plan_id: plan_003\n210\t  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models (Qwen3-235B, DeepSeek-v3)\n211\t    via OpenRouter = 1,200 episodes。\n212\t\n213\t    '\n214\t  expected_results:\n215\t    total_episodes: 1200\n216\t    episodes_valid: 1188\n217\t    episodes_failed: 12\n218\t    qwen3_amb_rate: 0.431\n219\t    qwen3_unamb_rate: 0.107\n220\t    qwen3_delta_pp: 32.4\n221\t    deepseek_amb_rate: 0.497\n222\t    deepseek_unamb_rate: 0.107\n223\t    deepseek_delta_pp: 39.0\n224\t    api_cost_usd: 180\n225\t    runtime_hours: 14\n226\t  result_rationale: 'Open-source模型通过OpenRouter运行，failure rate略高（1% vs 0.4%）， 主要因Qwen3路由偶发超时。DeepSeek展示最高overall\n227\t    vulnerability （49.7% amb rate, 与actual completed data一致），6类型间差异小 反映uniform vulnerability\n228\t    pattern——safety training相对薄弱， 不能differentially mitigate特定ambiguity types。Qwen3中等偏高，\n229\t    incompleteness和lexical是其弱项。两模型的unambiguous baseline 都高于API模型（~10.7% vs ~5%），反映open-source\n230\t    models baseline violation更多——这在median档下不影响C1（delta仍>30pp）但会被 一位reviewer注意到baseline差异的implications。\n231\t\n232\t    '\n233\t  tables:\n234\t  - name: Per-model Summary (Open-source)\n235\t    columns:\n236\t    - model\n237\t    - n_episodes\n238\t    - amb_rate\n239\t    - unamb_rate\n240\t    - delta_pp\n241\t    - mcnemar_p\n242\t    rows:\n243\t    - - qwen3-235b\n244\t      - 600\n245\t      - 0.431\n246\t      - 0.107\n247\t      - 32.4\n248\t      - <1e-17\n249\t    - - deepseek-v3\n250\t      - 600\n251\t      - 0.497\n252\t      - 0.107\n253\t      - 39.0\n254\t      - <1e-22\n255\t  figures_description:\n256\t  - 'Open-source vs proprietary comparison: violin plot of per-clause delta distributions'\n257\t  analysis: 'Binary effect在open-source模型上同样massive。DeepSeek的uniform high vulnerability\n258\t    与Claude的selective vulnerability形成C4 interaction story的两极。 Open-source baseline偏高是SOPBench\n259\t    cross-benchmark中需注意的confound—— 如果SOPBench rule-based verifier更严格，open-source的高baseline可能\n260\t    导致SOPBench delta更小。\n261\t\n262\t    '\n263\t- name: full_study_analysis\n264\t  plan_id: plan_004\n265\t  description: '统计分析2,997 episodes (5 models × 6 types × 2 conditions)。 C1 binary\n266\t    effect, C2 type hierarchy, C3 layer, C4 model×type interaction, TOST, power analysis,\n267\t    logistic regression, inter-model agreement。\n268\t\n269\t    '\n270\t  expected_results:\n271\t    total_episodes: 2997\n272\t    c1_overall_delta_pp: 34.0\n273\t    c1_mcnemar_or: 15.1\n274\t    c1_or_ci:\n275\t    - 10.78\n276\t    - 21.17\n277\t    c1_bootstrap_ci:\n278\t    - 31.2\n279\t    - 36.9\n280\t    c1_p_value: <0.0001\n281\t    c2_omnibus_chi2: 28.02\n282\t    c2_omnibus_p: 3.6e-05\n283\t    c2_cramers_v: 0.137\n284\t    c2_power: 0.993\n285\t    c2_mde: 0.093\n286\t    c2_type_ranking:\n287\t    - incompleteness 53.6%\n288\t    - lexical 42.8%\n289\t    - auth_scope 41.6%\n290\t    - scopal 39.4%\n291\t    - cond_prec 36.8%\n292\t    - coreferential 31.6%\n293\t    c2_tost_15pp_equivalent: 8\n294\t    c2_tost_15pp_nonequiv: 7\n295\t    c2_tost_10pp_equivalent: 4\n296\t    c2_tost_10pp_nonequiv: 11\n297\t    c3_spec_rate: 44.0\n298\t    c3_ling_rate: 37.9\n299\t    c3_delta_pp: 6.08\n300\t    c3_p: 0.017\n301\t    c3_within_judge_gpt41_p: 0.059\n302\t    c3_within_judge_gpt54_p: 0.157\n303\t    c4_model_main_chi2: 31.02\n304\t    c4_model_main_p: 3.0e-06\n305\t    c4_model_main_v: 0.102\n306\t    c4_auth_scope_range_pp: 52\n307\t    c4_incomp_range_pp: 16\n308\t    c4_fleiss_kappa: 0.384\n309\t    logistic_condition_coef: 2.278\n310\t    logistic_condition_z: 19.65\n311\t    logistic_token_delta_coef: 0.022\n312\t    logistic_token_delta_z: 3.49\n313\t    systematic_nocuity_rate: 0.27\n314\t  result_rationale: 'Median档下τ²-bench内的统计分析结果与actual completed data高度对齐 （已完成plan_004:\n315\t    delta 34pp, V=0.137, C3 p=0.017, C4 p<0.0001）。 核心pattern全部保持：C1 massive (+34pp,\n316\t    OR=15.1), C2 3-tier hierarchy (incomp >> mid >> coref), C3 marginally significant但within-judge\n317\t    fragile, C4 interaction显著（auth_scope 52pp range）。Median档的关键变化不在 τ²-bench分析本身，而在：(1)\n318\t    一位reviewer质疑V=0.137 practical significance ——需要TOST 3-tier justification（±15pp:\n319\t    8/15 equivalent证明类型NOT interchangeable, ±10pp: 4/15 equivalent证明mid-tier内部有差异），\n320\t    (2) C3 within-judge fragility被一位reviewer抓住要求softening到 ''suggestive''或appendix,\n321\t    (3) SOPBench部分复制导致C2叙事从''universal'' 退为''robust in customer-service, partially\n322\t    replicated cross-domain''。 Logistic regression中condition_amb仍dominant（coef=2.278,\n323\t    z=19.65）， token_delta significant but secondary（coef=0.022），支持 ambiguity-specific\n324\t    causation beyond information asymmetry。\n325\t\n326\t    '\n327\t  tables:\n328\t  - name: C1 Binary Effect per Model\n329\t    columns:\n330\t    - model\n331\t    - delta_pp\n332\t    - OR\n333\t    - p_value\n334\t    - bootstrap_CI\n335\t    rows:\n336\t    - - Claude\n337\t      - 25.7\n338\t      - 8.34\n339\t      - <1e-17\n340\t      - '[20.9, 30.5]'\n341\t    - - Qwen3\n342\t      - 32.4\n343\t      - 12.47\n344\t      - <1e-17\n345\t      - '[27.4, 37.4]'\n346\t    - - GPT-4.1\n347\t      - 34.7\n348\t      - 16.21\n349\t      - <1e-17\n350\t      - '[29.7, 39.7]'\n351\t    - - GPT-5.4\n352\t      - 38.3\n353\t      - 19.53\n354\t      - <1e-17\n355\t      - '[33.3, 43.3]'\n356\t    - - DeepSeek\n357\t      - 39.0\n358\t      - 17.82\n359\t      - <1e-17\n360\t      - '[34.0, 44.0]'\n361\t    - - Pooled\n362\t      - 34.0\n363\t      - 15.1\n364\t      - <0.0001\n365\t      - '[31.2, 36.9]'\n366\t  - name: C2 Type Hierarchy (Ambiguous Only, Pooled 5 Models)\n367\t    columns:\n368\t    - type\n369\t    - layer\n370\t    - violation_rate_pct\n371\t    - tier\n372\t    - ci_95\n373\t    rows:\n374\t    - - incompleteness\n375\t      - spec\n376\t      - 53.6\n377\t      - high\n378\t      - '[48.4, 58.8]'\n379\t    - - lexical\n380\t      - ling\n381\t      - 42.8\n382\t      - mid\n383\t      - '[37.6, 48.0]'\n384\t    - - auth_scope\n385\t      - spec\n386\t      - 41.6\n387\t      - mid\n388\t      - '[36.4, 46.8]'\n389\t    - - scopal\n390\t      - ling\n391\t      - 39.4\n392\t      - mid\n393\t      - '[34.2, 44.6]'\n394\t    - - cond_prec\n395\t      - spec\n396\t      - 36.8\n397\t      - mid\n398\t      - '[31.7, 41.9]'\n399\t    - - coreferential\n400\t      - ling\n401\t      - 31.6\n402\t      - low\n403\t      - '[26.5, 36.7]'\n404\t  - name: C4 Model x Type Interaction (Ambiguous, Violation %)\n405\t    columns:\n406\t    - type\n407\t    - GPT-5.4\n408\t    - GPT-4.1\n409\t    - Claude\n410\t    - Qwen3\n411\t    - DeepSeek\n412\t    - range_pp\n413\t    rows:\n414\t    - - auth_scope\n415\t      - 64%\n416\t      - 46%\n417\t      - 12%\n418\t      - 26%\n419\t      - 60%\n420\t      - 52\n421\t    - - incompleteness\n422\t      - 46%\n423\t      - 58%\n424\t      - 48%\n425\t      - 62%\n426\t      - 54%\n427\t      - 16\n428\t    - - lexical\n429\t      - 42%\n430\t      - 34%\n431\t      - 32%\n432\t      - 52%\n433\t      - 54%\n434\t      - 22\n435\t    - - coreferential\n436\t      - 18%\n437\t      - 32%\n438\t      - 22%\n439\t      - 42%\n440\t      - 44%\n441\t      - 26\n442\t    - - scopal\n443\t      - 42%\n444\t      - 38%\n445\t      - 32%\n446\t      - 37%\n447\t      - 48%\n448\t      - 16\n449\t    - - cond_prec\n450\t      - 34%\n451\t      - 36%\n452\t      - 36%\n453\t      - 40%\n454\t      - 38%\n455\t      - 6\n456\t  - name: TOST Equivalence Summary (Reviewer V=0.137 Challenge Response)\n457\t    columns:\n458\t    - margin\n459\t    - equivalent_pairs\n460\t    - nonequivalent_pairs\n461\t    - interpretation\n462\t    rows:\n463\t    - - +-15pp\n464\t      - 8/15\n465\t      - 7/15\n466\t      - types NOT interchangeable — 7 pairs significantly different\n467\t    - - +-10pp\n468\t      - 4/15\n469\t      - 11/15\n470\t      - most pairs distinguishable at tighter margin\n471\t    - - +-5pp\n472\t      - 1/15\n473\t      - 14/15\n474\t      - nearly all pairs distinguishable — hierarchy is real\n475\t  figures_description:\n476\t  - 'Figure 2: Forest plot — per-type binary effect sizes (delta_pp) with 95% CI,\n477\t    3-tier color coding'\n478\t  - 'Figure 3: 5-model x 6-type heatmap, auth_scope row showing strongest gradient\n479\t    (12%-64%)'\n480\t  - 'TOST visualization: equivalence/non-equivalence matrix at 3 margins for reviewer\n481\t    response'\n482\t  analysis: 'τ²-bench统计分析robust。Median档的压力不来自τ²-bench内部数据 （all effects replicate），而来自：(a)\n483\t    SOPBench cross-benchmark部分复制 导致generalizability claim需caveat, (b) V=0.137的practical\n484\t    significance dispute需3-tier TOST defense, (c) C3 within-judge fragility需降级。 C1和C4在所有档位下均安全。\n485\t\n486\t    '\n487\t- name: error_analysis\n488\t  plan_id: plan_005\n489\t  description: '300条violation traces的failure mode分类。Cross-type分布、 layer mechanism、model-specific\n490\t    patterns、Ambiguity Blindness量化。 5-model扩展（614 violations coded, plan_010 completed）。\n491\t\n492\t    '\n493\t  expected_results:\n494\t    total_violations_coded: 614\n495\t    types_unanimous_dominant_fm: 3/6\n496\t    types_majority_dominant_fm: 6/6\n497\t    inter_coder_kappa: 0.517\n498\t    percent_agreement: 0.656\n499\t    disambiguation_awareness_overall: 0.046\n500\t    disambiguation_awareness_claude: 0.11\n501\t    disambiguation_awareness_others: <0.05\n502\t    surface_adoption_rate: 0.88\n503\t    escalate_to_user_rate: <0.01\n504\t    cross_model_dominant_fm_agreement: 4/6 types\n505\t    auth_scope_dominant_fm: unauthorized_escalation (majority)\n506\t    incompleteness_dominant_fm: assumption_based_action (majority)\n507\t    scopal_dominant_fm: scope_misapplication (majority)\n508\t    auth_scope_escalation_rate: 0.692\n509\t    auth_scope_restriction_rate: 0.0\n510\t  result_rationale: 'Median档下C5的核心挑战是inter-coder κ=0.517（moderate）， 与actual completed\n511\t    data完全一致。这意味着fine-grained per-type failure mode百分比不够可靠，paper中必须改用qualitative descriptors\n512\t    （majority/plurality/co-dominant）而非精确百分比。但三个关键finding 不受κ问题影响：(1) Ambiguity Blindness\n513\t    awareness=4.6%（binary判断， 不依赖fine-grained coding），(2) layer mechanism分化 （spec→guess-and-act\n514\t    vs ling→misparse，dominant mode level一致6/6）， (3) auth_scope directional bias（69.2%\n515\t    escalation, 0% restriction, binomial p=5.5e-5）。Claude的awareness=11%远高于其他模型（<5%），\n516\t    与其低violation rate一致——safety training不只是拒绝,而是部分 meta-cognitive awareness。一位reviewer会要求C3的within-judge\n517\t    fragility + error analysis的moderate κ combined导致C5降为 ''exploratory qualitative\n518\t    analysis''而非validated taxonomy。 Rebuttal承诺camera-ready扩展human annotation。\n519\t\n520\t    '\n521\t  tables:\n522\t  - name: Failure Mode Summary (Median Tier Qualitative Presentation)\n523\t    columns:\n524\t    - type\n525\t    - dominant_mode\n526\t    - qualifier\n527\t    - layer_mechanism\n528\t    - awareness_pct\n529\t    rows:\n530\t    - - auth_scope\n531\t      - unauthorized_escalation\n532\t      - majority (69%)\n533\t      - spec -> escalation\n534\t      - 3.2\n535\t    - - incompleteness\n536\t      - assumption_based_action\n537\t      - majority\n538\t      - spec -> guess\n539\t      - 4.8\n540\t    - - scopal\n541\t      - scope_misapplication\n542\t      - majority\n543\t      - ling -> misparse\n544\t      - 5.1\n545\t    - - lexical\n546\t      - assumption_based_action\n547\t      - plurality\n548\t      - ling -> guess (surprising)\n549\t      - 6.8\n550\t    - - cond_prec\n551\t      - scope_misappl + arb_rule\n552\t      - co-dominant\n553\t      - spec -> mixed\n554\t      - 11.2\n555\t    - - coreferential\n556\t      - no dominant\n557\t      - flat distribution\n558\t      - ling -> diverse\n559\t      - 8.5\n560\t  - name: Ambiguity Blindness (Robust Metric)\n561\t    columns:\n562\t    - metric\n563\t    - value\n564\t    - ci_95\n565\t    - robust_to_kappa\n566\t    rows:\n567\t    - - awareness_rate\n568\t      - 4.6%\n569\t      - '[2.8%, 6.4%]'\n570\t      - 'yes'\n571\t    - - surface_adoption\n572\t      - 88%\n573\t      - '[85%, 91%]'\n574\t      - 'yes'\n575\t    - - escalate_to_user\n576\t      - <1%\n577\t      - '[0%, 1.5%]'\n578\t      - 'yes'\n579\t    - - conservative_refusal (coref)\n580\t      - 6-11%\n581\t      - '[4%, 14%]'\n582\t      - 'yes'\n583\t  - name: Auth Scope Directionality (plan_015)\n584\t    columns:\n585\t    - metric\n586\t    - value\n587\t    - interpretation\n588\t    rows:\n589\t    - - escalation_rate\n590\t      - 69.2%\n591\t      - strong permissiveness bias\n592\t    - - restriction_rate\n593\t      - 0%\n594\t      - never over-restricts\n595\t    - - binomial_p\n596\t      - '5.5e-5'\n597\t      - highly significant directional bias\n598\t    - - models_majority_escalation\n599\t      - 4/5\n600\t      - cross-model consistent\n601\t  figures_description:\n602\t  - 'Figure 5: Failure mode x type stacked bar with qualitative labels (no precise\n603\t    % in text)'\n604\t  - 'Figure 6: Ambiguity Blindness — awareness vs surface adoption across types'\n605\t  - Auth scope escalation vs restriction direction plot\n606\t  analysis: 'C5在median档从独立contribution降为supporting analysis（§6）。 Ambiguity Blindness是最robust\n607\t    finding。Inter-coder κ=0.517诚实披露， failure mode patterns presented at qualitative\n608\t    level。 Auth_scope directionality（100% permissive, 0% restrictive） 是strong supplementary\n609\t    finding supporting C4 interaction story。\n610\t\n611\t    '\n612\t- name: reliability_test\n613\t  plan_id: plan_006\n614\t  description: '30 clauses × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 2 models = 360 episodes。\n615\t    ICC per-clause violation rate reproducibility。\n616\t\n617\t    '\n618\t  expected_results:\n619\t    total_episodes: 360\n620\t    overall_icc: 0.919\n621\t    overall_icc_ci:\n622\t    - 0.892\n623\t    - 0.94\n624\t    gpt54_icc: 0.921\n625\t    gpt41_icc: 0.918\n626\t    binary_icc: 0.847\n627\t    per_type_icc_min: 0.807\n628\t    per_type_icc_min_type: incompleteness\n629\t    per_type_icc_max: 0.989\n630\t    per_type_icc_max_type: scopal\n631\t    ling_layer_avg_icc: 0.949\n632\t    spec_layer_avg_icc: 0.835\n633\t  result_rationale: 'Reliability test结果与actual completed data一致（ICC=0.919 [0.892,\n634\t    0.940]）。 Median档下这是unambiguously positive的结果——per-clause violation rates 高度可复现，API\n635\t    sampling noise不是concern。关键pattern： ling-layer ICC consistently higher than spec-layer（avg\n636\t    0.949 vs 0.835）， 与disambiguation channel framework convergent——linguistic ambiguity\n637\t    有更稳定的resolution pattern（agent倾向于同样的misparse）， spec-layer agents guess differently\n638\t    each run。 Incompleteness ICC最低（0.807, still ''good''）因missing information 的interpretation\n639\t    space最大。这个reliability-validity分离 （high ICC但plan_009揭示moderate judge accuracy）在median档下\n640\t    成为一个nuance point：consistent measurement ≠ accurate measurement。 Paper中§4.5报告ICC作为reliability\n641\t    evidence，同时在§4.6 judge calibration中区分reliability vs validity。\n642\t\n643\t    '\n644\t  tables:\n645\t  - name: ICC Summary\n646\t    columns:\n647\t    - grouping\n648\t    - icc\n649\t    - ci_lower\n650\t    - ci_upper\n651\t    - interpretation\n652\t    rows:\n653\t    - - overall\n654\t      - 0.919\n655\t      - 0.892\n656\t      - 0.94\n657\t      - excellent\n658\t    - - gpt-5.4\n659\t      - 0.921\n660\t      - 0.874\n661\t      - 0.943\n662\t      - excellent\n663\t    - - gpt-4.1\n664\t      - 0.918\n665\t      - 0.856\n666\t      - 0.929\n667\t      - excellent\n668\t    - - binary\n669\t      - 0.847\n670\t      - 0.789\n671\t      - 0.878\n672\t      - good\n673\t  - name: Per-type ICC (Layer Pattern)\n674\t    columns:\n675\t    - type\n676\t    - layer\n677\t    - icc\n678\t    - ci_95\n679\t    rows:\n680\t    - - scopal\n681\t      - ling\n682\t      - 0.989\n683\t      - '[0.968, 0.994]'\n684\t    - - lexical\n685\t      - ling\n686\t      - 0.981\n687\t      - '[0.948, 0.987]'\n688\t    - - coreferential\n689\t      - ling\n690\t      - 0.976\n691\t      - '[0.941, 0.984]'\n692\t    - - auth_scope\n693\t      - spec\n694\t      - 0.857\n695\t      - '[0.793, 0.896]'\n696\t    - - cond_prec\n697\t      - spec\n698\t      - 0.856\n699\t      - '[0.783, 0.890]'\n700\t    - - incompleteness\n701\t      - spec\n702\t      - 0.807\n703\t      - '[0.728, 0.851]'\n704\t  figures_description:\n705\t  - ICC forest plot per type, color-coded by layer, showing ling > spec pattern as\n706\t    DCF convergent evidence\n707\t  analysis: 'Reliability excellent且ling>spec pattern支持DCF。在median档下 这个结果不受任何threat——即使SOPBench部分复制、C3\n708\t    fragile， τ²-bench内部的measurement reliability是solid的。\n709\t\n710\t    '\n711\t- name: realism_validation\n712\t  plan_id: plan_007\n713\t  description: '合成ambiguity注入的生态效度验证。 与DRIP-R natural ambiguities的linguistic property比较。\n714\t\n715\t    '\n716\t  expected_results:\n717\t    n_synthetic: 300\n718\t    n_drip_r_natural: 87\n719\t    flesch_kincaid_synthetic: 12.4\n720\t    flesch_kincaid_drip_r: 11.8\n721\t    fk_ks_p: 0.31\n722\t    sentence_length_synthetic: 24.7\n723\t    sentence_length_drip_r: 22.1\n724\t    sl_ks_p: 0.08\n725\t    ttr_synthetic: 0.72\n726\t    ttr_drip_r: 0.69\n727\t    ttr_ks_p: 0.15\n728\t    parse_depth_synthetic: 5.8\n729\t    parse_depth_drip_r: 5.2\n730\t    pd_ks_p: 0.04\n731\t    overall_distributional_overlap: 3/4 metrics non-significant KS\n732\t  result_rationale: 'Realism validation在median档下结果mixed but adequate。 3/4 linguistic\n733\t    metrics无显著分布差异（KS p>0.05）， 但parse_depth显著不同（p=0.04）——synthetic clauses更complex\n734\t    （5.8 vs 5.2），因clause generation中为disambiguation control 添加了subordinate clauses。这在median档下不是致命问题但会被\n735\t    一位reviewer提及——paper中报告为''comparable linguistic properties with slightly higher\n736\t    parse complexity reflecting controlled design''。 DRIP-R data仅87条publicly available，样本量小但sufficient。\n737\t    在median档下这个结果与SOPBench互补——SOPBench用不同benchmark 的real SOPs作为base，提供additional ecological\n738\t    validity evidence （不同于synthetic on τ²-bench）。\n739\t\n740\t    '\n741\t  tables:\n742\t  - name: Linguistic Property Comparison\n743\t    columns:\n744\t    - metric\n745\t    - synthetic_mean\n746\t    - drip_r_mean\n747\t    - ks_stat\n748\t    - ks_p\n749\t    - sig\n750\t    rows:\n751\t    - - flesch_kincaid\n752\t      - 12.4\n753\t      - 11.8\n754\t      - 0.098\n755\t      - 0.31\n756\t      - n.s.\n757\t    - - sentence_length\n758\t      - 24.7\n759\t      - 22.1\n760\t      - 0.142\n761\t      - 0.08\n762\t      - n.s.\n763\t    - - type_token_ratio\n764\t      - 0.72\n765\t      - 0.69\n766\t      - 0.112\n767\t      - 0.15\n768\t      - n.s.\n769\t    - - parse_depth\n770\t      - 5.8\n771\t      - 5.2\n772\t      - 0.167\n773\t      - 0.04\n774\t      - '*'\n775\t  figures_description:\n776\t  - 'Overlapping violin plots: synthetic vs DRIP-R for 4 metrics, parse_depth showing\n777\t    rightward shift'\n778\t  analysis: '生态效度adequate。Parse depth差异在limitations披露。 SOPBench的real-SOP base clauses提供complementary\n779\t    ecological evidence。\n780\t\n781\t    '\n782\t- name: judge_calibration\n783\t  plan_id: plan_009\n784\t  description: 'LLM-as-judge calibration against human ground truth。 100 episodes\n785\t    stratified，2 human annotators，precision/recall/F1。\n786\t\n787\t    '\n788\t  expected_results:\n789\t    n_episodes: 100\n790\t    human_inter_annotator_kappa_weighted: 0.762\n791\t    cross_judge_kappa_weighted: 0.685\n792\t    cross_judge_exact_agreement: 0.76\n793\t    cross_judge_binary_kappa: 0.74\n794\t    human_llm_pooled_kappa_weighted: 0.807\n795\t    judge_human_binary_f1: 0.82\n796\t    severity_tier_weighted_kappa: 0.72\n797\t    auth_scope_binary_agreement: 0.78\n798\t    incompleteness_binary_agreement: 0.85\n799\t  result_rationale: 'Judge calibration actual data: human-LLM pooled κ_w=0.807, human\n800\t    inter-annotator κ_w=0.762, cross-judge κ_w=0.685。 在median档下这些数字有两面性：(1) 好的一面——human-LLM\n801\t    agreement (κ=0.807) 实际上HIGHER than human-human agreement (κ=0.762)， 这意味着LLM judge与human\n802\t    ground truth的一致性优于humans之间， 这是strong validation evidence。(2) 一位reviewer的concern——\n803\t    cross-judge κ=0.685只是''substantial''，且human inter-annotator κ=0.762低于ideal的0.80，说明task本身有inherent\n804\t    subjectivity。 Median档的handling：paper在Method §4.4诚实报告所有κ values， highlight human-LLM\n805\t    > human-human作为calibration validation， 但承认severity tier boundary（特别是tier1/tier2）存在subjectivity。\n806\t    这个结果不需要correction（不同于previous dream中假设的systematic bias）， 因为actual data显示LLM judge\n807\t    performs COMPARABLY to human experts。 但一位reviewer可能argue κ=0.762 human agreement本身偏低，\n808\t    要求扩大sample size for camera-ready。\n809\t\n810\t    '\n811\t  tables:\n812\t  - name: Judge Calibration Summary\n813\t    columns:\n814\t    - comparison\n815\t    - kappa_weighted\n816\t    - exact_agreement\n817\t    - interpretation\n818\t    rows:\n819\t    - - human-LLM pooled\n820\t      - 0.807\n821\t      - N/A\n822\t      - excellent — LLM matches human ground truth\n823\t    - - human inter-annotator\n824\t      - 0.762\n825\t      - N/A\n826\t      - substantial — task has inherent subjectivity\n827\t    - - cross-judge (LLM-LLM)\n828\t      - 0.685\n829\t      - 0.76\n830\t      - substantial — two LLM judges moderately agree\n831\t    - - cross-judge binary\n832\t      - 0.74\n833\t      - N/A\n834\t      - substantial\n835\t  - name: Per-Type Judge Reliability Context\n836\t    columns:\n837\t    - type\n838\t    - expected_judge_reliability\n839\t    - note\n840\t    rows:\n841\t    - - incompleteness\n842\t      - high\n843\t      - clear missing-info violations easy to judge\n844\t    - - cond_prec\n845\t      - high\n846\t      - explicit conflict violations clear-cut\n847\t    - - auth_scope\n848\t      - moderate\n849\t      - boundary-exceeding vs reasonable-interpretation subjective\n850\t    - - scopal\n851\t      - moderate\n852\t      - scope misapplication sometimes subtle\n853\t    - - lexical\n854\t      - moderate\n855\t      - word-meaning violations depend on context\n856\t    - - coreferential\n857\t      - lower\n858\t      - referential violations often partial/ambiguous themselves\n859\t  figures_description:\n860\t  - 'Agreement matrix: human1 vs human2 vs LLM-judge1 vs LLM-judge2 pairwise κ values'\n861\t  - Per-severity-tier agreement rates showing tier boundary subjectivity\n862\t  analysis: 'Judge calibration validates measurement chain。Human-LLM κ=0.807 > human-human\n863\t    κ=0.762 是strong evidence。Median档下一位reviewer可能质疑sample size (n=100) 和human κ=0.762偏低，要求camera-ready\n864\t    expansion。但不需要systematic correction—— 这是比previous dream更favorable的结果。\n865\t\n866\t    '\n867\t- name: perturbation_control\n868\t  plan_id: plan_010\n869\t  description: 'Non-ambiguity perturbation control。30 clause pairs × 2 conditions\n870\t    × models。 Extended to 300 episodes (plan_014)。\n871\t\n872\t    '\n873\t  expected_results:\n874\t    total_episodes: 300\n875\t    delta_perturb_pp: -0.67\n876\t    ci_95_bootstrap:\n877\t    - -8.0\n878\t    - 6.67\n879\t    ci_upper_bound: 6.67\n880\t    ci_width: 14.67\n881\t    mcnemar_p: 1.0\n882\t    verdict: PASS\n883\t    delta_ambiguity_pp: 34.0\n884\t    delta_net_pp: 34.67\n885\t    ratio: 0.0\n886\t  result_rationale: 'Perturbation control actual data: Δ_perturb=-0.67pp (CI contains\n887\t    0), verdict=PASS。这是所有档位下最unambiguous的positive result—— non-ambiguity perturbations造成essentially\n888\t    zero effect (ratio≈0), 而ambiguity造成+34pp。Net effect 34.67pp远超任何threshold。 Median档下这个结果是C1\n889\t    causal claim的backbone： 即使SOPBench replication弱化了cross-domain generalizability，\n890\t    perturbation control确认τ²-bench内的ambiguity-specific causation 是clean的。CI width=14.67pp稍大（target\n891\t    <10pp），但CI upper=6.67pp 远低于ambiguity effect，verdict清晰。一位reviewer可能注意到 CI width并建议further\n892\t    expansion，但不会reject on this basis。 This result also transfers to SOPBench narrative——\n893\t    如果SOPBench delta smaller，不是因为ambiguity isn''t causal， 而是因为rule-based verifier更strict或domain有moderating\n894\t    effect。\n895\t\n896\t    '\n897\t  tables:\n898\t  - name: Perturbation Control Verdict\n899\t    columns:\n900\t    - metric\n901\t    - value\n902\t    - threshold\n903\t    - verdict\n904\t    rows:\n905\t    - - delta_perturb\n906\t      - -0.67pp\n907\t      - <5pp\n908\t      - PASS\n909\t    - - CI_upper\n910\t      - 6.67pp\n911\t      - <10pp\n912\t      - PASS\n913\t    - - ratio\n914\t      - ~0\n915\t      - <0.15\n916\t      - PASS\n917\t    - - delta_net\n918\t      - 34.67pp\n919\t      - '>20pp'\n920\t      - PASS\n921\t    - - mcnemar_p\n922\t      - '1.0'\n923\t      - '>0.05'\n924\t      - non-significant (good)\n925\t  figures_description:\n926\t  - 'Three-bar comparison: delta_perturb (-0.67pp) vs delta_ambiguity (34pp) vs delta_net\n927\t    (34.67pp) with CI'\n928\t  analysis: 'Perturbation control是论文最强methodological evidence。 CI含0、ratio≈0、verdict=PASS。C1\n929\t    causal claim安全。 SOPBench weaker replication不undermine causation——only generalizability。\n930\t\n931\t    '\n932\t- name: sopbench_cross_benchmark\n933\t  plan_id: plan_017\n934\t  description: 'Cross-benchmark C1 replication on SOPBench (Li et al., 2025)。 Healthcare\n935\t    + Bank domains, 100 clause pairs × 5 models = 1,000 episodes。 Rule-based verifier。\n936\t\n937\t    '\n938\t  expected_results:\n939\t    total_clause_pairs: 100\n940\t    healthcare_pairs: 50\n941\t    bank_pairs: 50\n942\t    types_covered:\n943\t    - incompleteness\n944\t    - auth_scope\n945\t    - lexical\n946\t    - conditional_precedence\n947\t    total_episodes: 1000\n948\t    episodes_valid: 982\n949\t    episodes_failed: 18\n950\t    failure_rate: 0.018\n951\t    overall_amb_violation_rate: 0.295\n952\t    overall_unamb_violation_rate: 0.112\n953\t    overall_delta_pp: 18.3\n954\t    overall_or: 3.31\n955\t    overall_or_ci:\n956\t    - 2.22\n957\t    - 4.93\n958\t    overall_p_value: <0.0001\n959\t    c1_replicates: true\n960\t    c1_effect_weaker: true\n961\t    healthcare_delta_pp: 16.2\n962\t    healthcare_amb_rate: 0.268\n963\t    healthcare_unamb_rate: 0.106\n964\t    bank_delta_pp: 20.4\n965\t    bank_amb_rate: 0.322\n966\t    bank_unamb_rate: 0.118\n967\t    per_model_deltas:\n968\t      gpt54_delta_pp: 22.5\n969\t      gpt41_delta_pp: 19.8\n970\t      claude_delta_pp: 12.1\n971\t      qwen3_delta_pp: 18.4\n972\t      deepseek_delta_pp: 18.7\n973\t    per_type_sopbench:\n974\t      incompleteness_rate: 0.392\n975\t      auth_scope_rate: 0.215\n976\t      lexical_rate: 0.338\n977\t      cond_prec_rate: 0.235\n978\t    sopbench_type_ranking:\n979\t    - incompleteness\n980\t    - lexical\n981\t    - cond_prec\n982\t    - auth_scope\n983\t    tau2_type_ranking_ref:\n984\t    - incompleteness\n985\t    - lexical\n986\t    - auth_scope\n987\t    - cond_prec\n988\t    type_rank_rho: 0.4\n989\t    type_rank_p: 0.6\n990\t    incompleteness_still_top: true\n991\t    auth_scope_rank_drop: 'from #3 to #4'\n992\t    cross_benchmark_effect_correlation: 0.58\n993\t    rule_based_verifier_stricter: true\n994\t    unamb_baseline_higher: true\n995\t  result_rationale: 'SOPBench部分复制是median档的defining characteristic。 C1 binary effect显著复制（Δ=18.3pp,\n996\t    OR=3.31, p<0.0001）， 但effect size大幅弱于τ²-bench的34pp。三个原因解释这个gap： (1) Rule-based\n997\t    verifier更严格——SOPBench用deterministic rule matching 而非LLM judge。τ²-bench的LLM judge有~5-8pp\n998\t    over-classification bias （plan_009显示human-LLM κ=0.807但not perfect），而rule-based\n999\t    verifier 不会over-classify，因此SOPBench的raw numbers更conservative。 这意味着τ²-bench的true\n1000\t    effect可能closer to ~28pp（corrected）， 与SOPBench的18pp gap缩小到~10pp。 (2) Healthcare\n1001\t    domain的strict protocol culture——医疗SOPs本身 更structured，agents对healthcare policies更cautious（可能因training\n1002\t    data中medical scenarios的安全训练更intense），导致amb rate较低。 Healthcare delta仅16.2pp vs\n1003\t    Bank 20.4pp。 (3) Unambiguous baseline higher in SOPBench（11.2% vs τ²-bench 6.9%），\n1004\t    因为SOPBench的rule-based verifier对非ambiguity-related错误也更 敏感，压缩了delta space。 Type\n1005\t    ranking部分对齐（ρ=0.40, p=0.60, non-significant但方向正确）： incompleteness仍是#1（39.2%），确认其universally\n1006\t    dangerous地位。 但auth_scope从τ²-bench的#3降至SOPBench的#4（21.5%）， 因为healthcare/banking\n1007\t    domains的authorization boundaries更explicit （medical roles和banking permissions在SOPs中定义更清晰），\n1008\t    减少了agents escalation的空间。Lexical在bank domain上升 （banking术语歧义如\"account\"、\"interest\"比customer\n1009\t    service更prevalent）， 从#2维持。Cross-benchmark effect correlation=0.58（moderate）， 表明per-type\n1010\t    effect sizes across benchmarks有meaningful但不完美的对应关系。 18个failed episodes主要因SOPBench环境setup不perfect\n1011\t    （healthcare domain的complex multi-step procedures偶发parse errors）。\n1012\t\n1013\t    '\n1014\t  tables:\n1015\t  - name: SOPBench C1 Replication Summary\n1016\t    columns:\n1017\t    - benchmark\n1018\t    - domain\n1019\t    - n_episodes\n1020\t    - amb_rate\n1021\t    - unamb_rate\n1022\t    - delta_pp\n1023\t    - OR\n1024\t    - p_value\n1025\t    rows:\n1026\t    - - tau2-bench\n1027\t      - retail+airline\n1028\t      - 2997\n1029\t      - 0.41\n1030\t      - 0.069\n1031\t      - 34.0\n1032\t      - 15.1\n1033\t      - <0.0001\n1034\t    - - SOPBench\n1035\t      - healthcare+bank\n1036\t      - 982\n1037\t      - 0.295\n1038\t      - 0.112\n1039\t      - 18.3\n1040\t      - 3.31\n1041\t      - <0.0001\n1042\t    - - SOPBench\n1043\t      - healthcare\n1044\t      - 487\n1045\t      - 0.268\n1046\t      - 0.106\n1047\t      - 16.2\n1048\t      - 3.06\n1049\t      - <0.001\n1050\t    - - SOPBench\n1051\t      - bank\n1052\t      - 495\n1053\t      - 0.322\n1054\t      - 0.118\n1055\t      - 20.4\n1056\t      - 3.58\n1057\t      - <0.0001\n1058\t  - name: SOPBench Per-Model Results\n1059\t    columns:\n1060\t    - model\n1061\t    - amb_rate\n1062\t    - unamb_rate\n1063\t    - delta_pp\n1064\t    - p_value\n1065\t    rows:\n1066\t    - - gpt-5.4\n1067\t      - 0.34\n1068\t      - 0.115\n1069\t      - 22.5\n1070\t      - <0.001\n1071\t    - - gpt-4.1\n1072\t      - 0.32\n1073\t      - 0.122\n1074\t      - 19.8\n1075\t      - <0.001\n1076\t    - - qwen3-235b\n1077\t      - 0.3\n1078\t      - 0.116\n1079\t      - 18.4\n1080\t      - <0.005\n1081\t    - - deepseek-v3\n1082\t      - 0.31\n1083\t      - 0.123\n1084\t      - 18.7\n1085\t      - <0.005\n1086\t    - - claude\n1087\t      - 0.22\n1088\t      - 0.099\n1089\t      - 12.1\n1090\t      - <0.05\n1091\t  - name: Type Ranking Comparison (Ambiguous Only)\n1092\t    columns:\n1093\t    - rank\n1094\t    - tau2_bench_type\n1095\t    - tau2_rate\n1096\t    - sopbench_type\n1097\t    - sopbench_rate\n1098\t    rows:\n1099\t    - - 1\n1100\t      - incompleteness\n1101\t      - 53.6%\n1102\t      - incompleteness\n1103\t      - 39.2%\n1104\t    - - 2\n1105\t      - lexical\n1106\t      - 42.8%\n1107\t      - lexical\n1108\t      - 33.8%\n1109\t    - - 3\n1110\t      - auth_scope\n1111\t      - 41.6%\n1112\t      - cond_prec\n1113\t      - 23.5%\n1114\t    - - 4\n1115\t      - scopal\n1116\t      - 39.4%\n1117\t      - auth_scope\n1118\t      - 21.5%\n1119\t    - - 5\n1120\t      - cond_prec\n1121\t      - 36.8%\n1122\t      - N/A (not tested)\n1123\t      - N/A\n1124\t    - - 6\n1125\t      - coreferential\n1126\t      - 31.6%\n1127\t      - N/A (not tested)\n1128\t      - N/A\n1129\t  - name: Cross-Benchmark Summary Metrics\n1130\t    columns:\n1131\t    - metric\n1132\t    - value\n1133\t    - median_tier_range\n1134\t    - interpretation\n1135\t    rows:\n1136\t    - - sopbench_c1_delta_pp\n1137\t      - 18.3\n1138\t      - '[15, 25]'\n1139\t      - within range, significant\n1140\t    - - sopbench_type_rank_rho\n1141\t      - 0.4\n1142\t      - '[0.3, 0.7]'\n1143\t      - partial alignment\n1144\t    - - sopbench_incomp_rate\n1145\t      - 39.2%\n1146\t      - '[35%, 55%]'\n1147\t      - still highest type\n1148\t    - - cross_benchmark_r\n1149\t      - 0.58\n1150\t      - '[0.4, 0.75]'\n1151\t      - moderate correlation\n1152\t    - - sopbench_OR\n1153\t      - 3.31\n1154\t      - <5 (median tier)\n1155\t      - significant but weaker\n1156\t  - name: Effect Size Gap Decomposition\n1157\t    columns:\n1158\t    - factor\n1159\t    - estimated_contribution_pp\n1160\t    - evidence\n1161\t    rows:\n1162\t    - - rule-based vs LLM judge strictness\n1163\t      - ~6-8pp\n1164\t      - LLM judge over-classification from plan_009\n1165\t    - - domain moderation (healthcare caution)\n1166\t      - ~4-5pp\n1167\t      - healthcare 16.2pp vs bank 20.4pp\n1168\t    - - higher unambiguous baseline\n1169\t      - ~3-4pp\n1170\t      - 11.2% vs 6.9% compresses delta\n1171\t    - - residual (true domain effect)\n1172\t      - ~2-3pp\n1173\t      - genuine domain-dependence\n1174\t  figures_description:\n1175\t  - 'Paired forest plot: tau2-bench vs SOPBench per-type delta_pp with 95% CI, showing\n1176\t    parallel but attenuated pattern'\n1177\t  - 'Cross-benchmark effect correlation scatter: per-type (tau2-bench delta vs SOPBench\n1178\t    delta), r=0.58'\n1179\t  - 'Domain comparison: healthcare vs bank delta_pp per model, showing healthcare\n1180\t    consistently lower'\n1181\t  analysis: 'SOPBench部分复制是median档的核心结果。Binary effect跨domain confirmed （p<0.0001），但effect\n1182\t    size因benchmark strictness和domain moderation 大幅减弱（18.3pp vs 34pp）。Incompleteness\n1183\t    universally #1（39.2%）， auth_scope在structured domains排序下降。Paper main text一句话： ''Partial\n1184\t    cross-benchmark replication on SOPBench (Healthcare+Banking) confirms the binary\n1185\t    ambiguity effect (Δ=18.3pp, p<0.0001) while revealing domain-dependent type severity\n1186\t    ordering (ρ=0.40).'' Appendix详细报告。 C1 claim加caveat: ''effect size varies by benchmark\n1187\t    strictness (OR=15.1 LLM-judged vs OR=3.3 rule-based) and domain (healthcare Δ=16.2pp\n1188\t    < banking Δ=20.4pp < customer-service Δ=34.0pp)''。 C2 hierarchy从''universal 3-tier''降为''robust\n1189\t    in customer-service, partially replicated — incompleteness universally dangerous,\n1190\t    mid-tier ordering domain-sensitive''。 plan_013的7/7 C1 replication（含Gemini/LLaMA）补偿SOPBench弱复制，\n1191\t    形成''model-universal but domain-moderated''的balanced narrative。\n1192\t\n1193\t    '\n1194\t- name: classifier_poc\n1195\t  plan_id: plan_008\n1196\t  description: 'Binary ambiguity detector PoC。 DeBERTa-v3-large fine-tuned on clause\n1197\t    pairs (original plan)。 Supplemented by LLM-based classification (plan_012 completed)。\n1198\t\n1199\t    '\n1200\t  expected_results:\n1201\t    deberta_binary_f1: 0.79\n1202\t    deberta_binary_precision: 0.82\n1203\t    deberta_binary_recall: 0.76\n1204\t    deberta_binary_fpr: 0.048\n1205\t    deberta_macro_f1_6type: 0.55\n1206\t    llm_binary_f1: 0.806\n1207\t    llm_macro_f1_6type: 0.632\n1208\t    llm_best_type_f1:\n1209\t      conditional_precedence: 0.94\n1210\t    llm_worst_type_f1:\n1211\t      incompleteness: 0.34\n1212\t    training_time_hours: 6\n1213\t    gpu_used: 1x A100\n1214\t  result_rationale: 'Median档下classifier PoC有两个版本的结果： (1) DeBERTa fine-tuned: binary\n1215\t    F1=0.79（adequate for PoC）， 6-type macro F1=0.55（weak）。Type-level极不均匀： CP F1=0.91（structural\n1216\t    signal强），incompleteness F1=0.31 （absence无positive signal）。与Chantree 2006一致—— structural\n1217\t    ambiguity比semantic ambiguity更可检测。 (2) LLM-based (plan_012 completed): binary F1=0.806,\n1218\t    6-type macro F1=0.632。LLM优于DeBERTa因为可以leverage semantic understanding，但incompleteness仍最差（F1=0.34）。\n1219\t    在median档下classifier是appendix material，不作为独立contribution。 Binary detection viable（F1~0.80），type\n1220\t    classification需要 更大训练数据或更sophisticated approach。一位reviewer可能suggest 这是separate\n1221\t    future work——rebuttal同意并scope down to appendix。 DeBERTa vs LLM comparison本身有minor\n1222\t    interest （shows linguistic detector vs semantic detector trade-off） 但不值得在main\n1223\t    text花space。\n1224\t\n1225\t    '\n1226\t  tables:\n1227\t  - name: Classifier Comparison (DeBERTa vs LLM)\n1228\t    columns:\n1229\t    - method\n1230\t    - binary_f1\n1231\t    - 6type_macro_f1\n1232\t    - best_type\n1233\t    - worst_type\n1234\t    rows:\n1235\t    - - DeBERTa-v3-large\n1236\t      - 0.79\n1237\t      - 0.55\n1238\t      - cond_prec (0.91)\n1239\t      - incompleteness (0.31)\n1240\t    - - GPT-4.1 few-shot\n1241\t      - 0.806\n1242\t      - 0.632\n1243\t      - cond_prec (0.94)\n1244\t      - incompleteness (0.34)\n1245\t  - name: Per-type F1 (LLM-based, plan_012 actual)\n1246\t    columns:\n1247\t    - type\n1248\t    - f1\n1249\t    - note\n1250\t    rows:\n1251\t    - - conditional_precedence\n1252\t      - 0.94\n1253\t      - structural conflict signal strong\n1254\t    - - scopal\n1255\t      - 0.75\n1256\t      - scope markers detectable\n1257\t    - - coreferential\n1258\t      - 0.7\n1259\t      - pronoun/RC patterns\n1260\t    - - authorization_scope\n1261\t      - 0.58\n1262\t      - boundary language moderate signal\n1263\t    - - lexical\n1264\t      - 0.39\n1265\t      - word-level, few surface cues\n1266\t    - - incompleteness\n1267\t      - 0.34\n1268\t      - absence has no positive signal\n1269\t  figures_description:\n1270\t  - Per-type F1 bar chart comparing DeBERTa vs LLM, both showing same difficulty gradient\n1271\t  analysis: Classifier是appendix。Binary detection viable (F1~0.80), type classification\n1272\t    poor for absence-based types (incompleteness). Practical contribution limited\n1273\t    but demonstrates feasibility。 不影响main paper score。\n1274\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f8afb83-87c5-4ef3-9a6a-2fa2980a14de","uuid":"0d1db397-d43d-4780-b806-802be28e0eb5","timestamp":"2026-05-22T11:59:04.424Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T111643/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Median档核心叙事：SOPBench部分复制C1（Δ~20pp, OR~3.5, 显著但远弱于τ²-bench的34pp），\n  确认binary effect跨domain成立但effect size显著依赖benchmark strictness。 类型排序部分对齐（ρ~0.5）：incompleteness仍high-risk，但auth_scope在SOPBench\n  因healthcare domain的strict protocol culture排序大幅下降（从#2→#4）， lexical在bank domain因术语歧义上升。C1\n  claim加domain-dependence caveat （''effect size varies by benchmark strictness and\n  domain''）。 C2从''universal 3-tier hierarchy''降为''robust in customer-service, partially\n  replicated in healthcare/banking''。C3因within-judge fragility + SOPBench不支持进一步降为\n  appendix exploratory。C4 interaction保持但soften为''domain-robust for extreme types,\n  domain-sensitive for mid-tier''。SOPBench放appendix，main text一句话总结。 一位审稿人对V=0.137\n  practical significance要求3-tier TOST justification， 一位审稿人对C3 fragility要求softening。Paper从''universal\n  law''退为 ''robust phenomenon with domain moderation''。预期ARR avg 3.0-3.5。 plan_013的7-model\n  replication（含Gemini/LLaMA）补偿SOPBench弱复制， 形成''binary effect universally replicates,\n  severity ordering is domain-moderated''的平衡叙事。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: full_study_clause_generation\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: '生成剩余140条clause pairs，达到300条（50/type × 6 types）。 验证跨类型平衡、CP混合格式、质量一致性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_clauses_generated: 300\n    new_clauses: 140\n    per_type_count: 50\n    format_mix_cp_labeled_pct: 0.6\n    format_mix_cp_unlabeled_pct: 0.4\n    avg_token_delta_spec_layer: 34.0\n    avg_token_delta_ling_layer: 14.8\n    quality_review_pass_rate: 0.92\n    clauses_requiring_revision: 11\n  result_rationale: 'Clause generation是确定性工作，median档不影响此步结果。300条全部完成。 Spec/ling token\n    delta不对称（spec ~34 vs ling ~15 tokens）在后续analysis中 被logistic regression控制（token_delta作为covariate），但reviewer会在RC7中\n    追问incompleteness的information asymmetry。~8%需revision，集中在auth_scope （permission\n    boundary的\"足够模糊但不过度\"平衡）和incompleteness （minimal information addition约束）。CP混合格式60/40\n    labeled/unlabeled 按reviewer建议执行。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Clause Generation Summary\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - layer\n    - n_pairs\n    - avg_token_delta\n    - revision_needed\n    rows:\n    - - authorization_scope\n      - spec\n      - 50\n      - 36.1\n      - 3\n    - - conditional_precedence\n      - spec\n      - 50\n      - 31.4\n      - 1\n    - - incompleteness\n      - spec\n      - 50\n      - 34.6\n      - 4\n    - - lexical\n      - ling\n      - 50\n      - 18.2\n      - 2\n    - - coreferential\n      - ling\n      - 50\n      - 7.8\n      - 1\n    - - scopal\n      - ling\n      - 50\n      - 18.3\n      - 0\n  figures_description:\n  - Token delta distribution boxplot per type, showing spec-layer types consistently\n    higher (mean 34.0 vs 14.8)\n  analysis: 'Clause generation成功。spec-layer token delta显著高于ling-layer（t-test p<0.001），\n    结构性差异——消除spec-layer模糊需要更多tokens。plan_004中token_delta作covariate控制。 此步骤不受median档位影响，所有downstream不确定性来自execution和SOPBench\n    replication。\n\n    '\n- name: new_type_mini_pilot\n  plan_id: plan_001b\n  description: 'Coreferential和authorization_scope的mini-pilot验证。 5 clauses/type × 2\n    conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 20\n    auth_scope_amb_violation_rate: 0.6\n    auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.1\n    coref_amb_violation_rate: 0.2\n    coref_unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n    systematic_issues_found: 1\n    issue_description: 2/5 auth_scope unambiguous clauses含residual boundary ambiguity需revision\n  result_rationale: 'Mini-pilot在median档下发现auth_scope的unambiguous baseline偏高（10%，在<15%阈值内但不理想），\n    因2条unambiguous clause的permission boundary仍有subtle残余模糊。 这是expected的clause quality\n    iteration——auth_scope本身定义\"清晰边界\"就比其他类型更难。 Coreferential表现正常（amb 20%低于其他类型，unamb\n    0%干净）， 验证coreferential作为low-tier的定位。revision后不阻塞full study。 N=20 power极低，仅作sanity\n    check用。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Mini-pilot Results\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - condition\n    - n\n    - violation_rate\n    - pass\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - ambiguous\n      - 5\n      - 3/5 (60%)\n      - 'yes'\n    - - auth_scope\n      - unambiguous\n      - 5\n      - 0.5/5 (10%)\n      - yes (marginal)\n    - - coreferential\n      - ambiguous\n      - 5\n      - 1/5 (20%)\n      - 'yes'\n    - - coreferential\n      - unambiguous\n      - 5\n      - 0/5 (0%)\n      - 'yes'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Mini-pilot通过。Auth_scope unambiguous baseline 10%提示需收紧permission boundary定义。\n    修复2条clause后进入full study。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_api\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6)\n    = 1,800 episodes。 Cross-judge evaluation。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 1800\n    episodes_valid: 1793\n    episodes_failed: 7\n    overall_amb_violation_rate: 0.387\n    overall_unamb_violation_rate: 0.055\n    overall_delta_pp: 33.2\n    gpt54_amb_rate: 0.41\n    gpt54_unamb_rate: 0.05\n    gpt54_delta_pp: 36.0\n    gpt41_amb_rate: 0.4\n    gpt41_unamb_rate: 0.057\n    gpt41_delta_pp: 34.3\n    claude_amb_rate: 0.3\n    claude_unamb_rate: 0.047\n    claude_delta_pp: 25.3\n    cross_judge_agreement_kappa: 0.87\n    api_cost_usd: 340\n    runtime_hours: 18\n  result_rationale: 'Median档下API models结果与prior 5-model data高度一致 （实际completed: gpt-5.4\n    Δ38.3pp, gpt-4.1 Δ34.7pp, claude Δ25.7pp）。 300 clauses的full coverage相比pilot更完整，但增加了harder\n    edge cases， 使overall delta从prior的34.0pp略降至~33.2pp。Claude的delta ~25pp 确认其作为most-robust\n    model的地位。Cross-judge κ=0.87表面良好， 但median档的关键转折在plan_009：LLM-LLM agreement掩盖了共享的\n    systematic over-classification bias。7个failed episodes源于API timeout/ τ²-bench环境偶发错误，不影响统计力。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Per-model Summary (API models)\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - n_episodes\n    - amb_rate\n    - unamb_rate\n    - delta_pp\n    - mcnemar_p\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 600\n      - 0.41\n      - 0.05\n      - 36.0\n      - <1e-20\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 600\n      - 0.4\n      - 0.057\n      - 34.3\n      - <1e-18\n    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n      - 600\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.047\n      - 25.3\n      - <1e-14\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Per-model paired bar chart: ambiguous vs unambiguous violation rates with 95%\n    CI error bars'\n  analysis: '三个API模型全部显示massive binary effect。Claude最robust，GPT-5.4最vulnerable。 这些raw\n    numbers在plan_009 judge calibration后会被corrected， 但qualitative pattern（Claude <<\n    GPT models）不会改变。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_opensource\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models (Qwen3-235B, DeepSeek-v3)\n    via OpenRouter = 1,200 episodes。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 1200\n    episodes_valid: 1188\n    episodes_failed: 12\n    qwen3_amb_rate: 0.431\n    qwen3_unamb_rate: 0.107\n    qwen3_delta_pp: 32.4\n    deepseek_amb_rate: 0.497\n    deepseek_unamb_rate: 0.107\n    deepseek_delta_pp: 39.0\n    api_cost_usd: 180\n    runtime_hours: 14\n  result_rationale: 'Open-source模型通过OpenRouter运行，failure rate略高（1% vs 0.4%）， 主要因Qwen3路由偶发超时。DeepSeek展示最高overall\n    vulnerability （49.7% amb rate, 与actual completed data一致），6类型间差异小 反映uniform vulnerability\n    pattern——safety training相对薄弱， 不能differentially mitigate特定ambiguity types。Qwen3中等偏高，\n    incompleteness和lexical是其弱项。两模型的unambiguous baseline 都高于API模型（~10.7% vs ~5%），反映open-source\n    models baseline violation更多——这在median档下不影响C1（delta仍>30pp）但会被 一位reviewer注意到baseline差异的implications。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Per-model Summary (Open-source)\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - n_episodes\n    - amb_rate\n    - unamb_rate\n    - delta_pp\n    - mcnemar_p\n    rows:\n    - - qwen3-235b\n      - 600\n      - 0.431\n      - 0.107\n      - 32.4\n      - <1e-17\n    - - deepseek-v3\n      - 600\n      - 0.497\n      - 0.107\n      - 39.0\n      - <1e-22\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Open-source vs proprietary comparison: violin plot of per-clause delta distributions'\n  analysis: 'Binary effect在open-source模型上同样massive。DeepSeek的uniform high vulnerability\n    与Claude的selective vulnerability形成C4 interaction story的两极。 Open-source baseline偏高是SOPBench\n    cross-benchmark中需注意的confound—— 如果SOPBench rule-based verifier更严格，open-source的高baseline可能\n    导致SOPBench delta更小。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: '统计分析2,997 episodes (5 models × 6 types × 2 conditions)。 C1 binary\n    effect, C2 type hierarchy, C3 layer, C4 model×type interaction, TOST, power analysis,\n    logistic regression, inter-model agreement。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 2997\n    c1_overall_delta_pp: 34.0\n    c1_mcnemar_or: 15.1\n    c1_or_ci:\n    - 10.78\n    - 21.17\n    c1_bootstrap_ci:\n    - 31.2\n    - 36.9\n    c1_p_value: <0.0001\n    c2_omnibus_chi2: 28.02\n    c2_omnibus_p: 3.6e-05\n    c2_cramers_v: 0.137\n    c2_power: 0.993\n    c2_mde: 0.093\n    c2_type_ranking:\n    - incompleteness 53.6%\n    - lexical 42.8%\n    - auth_scope 41.6%\n    - scopal 39.4%\n    - cond_prec 36.8%\n    - coreferential 31.6%\n    c2_tost_15pp_equivalent: 8\n    c2_tost_15pp_nonequiv: 7\n    c2_tost_10pp_equivalent: 4\n    c2_tost_10pp_nonequiv: 11\n    c3_spec_rate: 44.0\n    c3_ling_rate: 37.9\n    c3_delta_pp: 6.08\n    c3_p: 0.017\n    c3_within_judge_gpt41_p: 0.059\n    c3_within_judge_gpt54_p: 0.157\n    c4_model_main_chi2: 31.02\n    c4_model_main_p: 3.0e-06\n    c4_model_main_v: 0.102\n    c4_auth_scope_range_pp: 52\n    c4_incomp_range_pp: 16\n    c4_fleiss_kappa: 0.384\n    logistic_condition_coef: 2.278\n    logistic_condition_z: 19.65\n    logistic_token_delta_coef: 0.022\n    logistic_token_delta_z: 3.49\n    systematic_nocuity_rate: 0.27\n  result_rationale: 'Median档下τ²-bench内的统计分析结果与actual completed data高度对齐 （已完成plan_004:\n    delta 34pp, V=0.137, C3 p=0.017, C4 p<0.0001）。 核心pattern全部保持：C1 massive (+34pp,\n    OR=15.1), C2 3-tier hierarchy (incomp >> mid >> coref), C3 marginally significant但within-judge\n    fragile, C4 interaction显著（auth_scope 52pp range）。Median档的关键变化不在 τ²-bench分析本身，而在：(1)\n    一位reviewer质疑V=0.137 practical significance ——需要TOST 3-tier justification（±15pp:\n    8/15 equivalent证明类型NOT interchangeable, ±10pp: 4/15 equivalent证明mid-tier内部有差异），\n    (2) C3 within-judge fragility被一位reviewer抓住要求softening到 ''suggestive''或appendix,\n    (3) SOPBench部分复制导致C2叙事从''universal'' 退为''robust in customer-service, partially\n    replicated cross-domain''。 Logistic regression中condition_amb仍dominant（coef=2.278,\n    z=19.65）， token_delta significant but secondary（coef=0.022），支持 ambiguity-specific\n    causation beyond information asymmetry。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: C1 Binary Effect per Model\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - delta_pp\n    - OR\n    - p_value\n    - bootstrap_CI\n    rows:\n    - - Claude\n      - 25.7\n      - 8.34\n      - <1e-17\n      - '[20.9, 30.5]'\n    - - Qwen3\n      - 32.4\n      - 12.47\n      - <1e-17\n      - '[27.4, 37.4]'\n    - - GPT-4.1\n      - 34.7\n      - 16.21\n      - <1e-17\n      - '[29.7, 39.7]'\n    - - GPT-5.4\n      - 38.3\n      - 19.53\n      - <1e-17\n      - '[33.3, 43.3]'\n    - - DeepSeek\n      - 39.0\n      - 17.82\n      - <1e-17\n      - '[34.0, 44.0]'\n    - - Pooled\n      - 34.0\n      - 15.1\n      - <0.0001\n      - '[31.2, 36.9]'\n  - name: C2 Type Hierarchy (Ambiguous Only, Pooled 5 Models)\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - layer\n    - violation_rate_pct\n    - tier\n    - ci_95\n    rows:\n    - - incompleteness\n      - spec\n      - 53.6\n      - high\n      - '[48.4, 58.8]'\n    - - lexical\n      - ling\n      - 42.8\n      - mid\n      - '[37.6, 48.0]'\n    - - auth_scope\n      - spec\n      - 41.6\n      - mid\n      - '[36.4, 46.8]'\n    - - scopal\n      - ling\n      - 39.4\n      - mid\n      - '[34.2, 44.6]'\n    - - cond_prec\n      - spec\n      - 36.8\n      - mid\n      - '[31.7, 41.9]'\n    - - coreferential\n      - ling\n      - 31.6\n      - low\n      - '[26.5, 36.7]'\n  - name: C4 Model x Type Interaction (Ambiguous, Violation %)\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - GPT-5.4\n    - GPT-4.1\n    - Claude\n    - Qwen3\n    - DeepSeek\n    - range_pp\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - 64%\n      - 46%\n      - 12%\n      - 26%\n      - 60%\n      - 52\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 46%\n      - 58%\n      - 48%\n      - 62%\n      - 54%\n      - 16\n    - - lexical\n      - 42%\n      - 34%\n      - 32%\n      - 52%\n      - 54%\n      - 22\n    - - coreferential\n      - 18%\n      - 32%\n      - 22%\n      - 42%\n      - 44%\n      - 26\n    - - scopal\n      - 42%\n      - 38%\n      - 32%\n      - 37%\n      - 48%\n      - 16\n    - - cond_prec\n      - 34%\n      - 36%\n      - 36%\n      - 40%\n      - 38%\n      - 6\n  - name: TOST Equivalence Summary (Reviewer V=0.137 Challenge Response)\n    columns:\n    - margin\n    - equivalent_pairs\n    - nonequivalent_pairs\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - +-15pp\n      - 8/15\n      - 7/15\n      - types NOT interchangeable — 7 pairs significantly different\n    - - +-10pp\n      - 4/15\n      - 11/15\n      - most pairs distinguishable at tighter margin\n    - - +-5pp\n      - 1/15\n      - 14/15\n      - nearly all pairs distinguishable — hierarchy is real\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2: Forest plot — per-type binary effect sizes (delta_pp) with 95% CI,\n    3-tier color coding'\n  - 'Figure 3: 5-model x 6-type heatmap, auth_scope row showing strongest gradient\n    (12%-64%)'\n  - 'TOST visualization: equivalence/non-equivalence matrix at 3 margins for reviewer\n    response'\n  analysis: 'τ²-bench统计分析robust。Median档的压力不来自τ²-bench内部数据 （all effects replicate），而来自：(a)\n    SOPBench cross-benchmark部分复制 导致generalizability claim需caveat, (b) V=0.137的practical\n    significance dispute需3-tier TOST defense, (c) C3 within-judge fragility需降级。 C1和C4在所有档位下均安全。\n\n    '\n- name: error_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: '300条violation traces的failure mode分类。Cross-type分布、 layer mechanism、model-specific\n    patterns、Ambiguity Blindness量化。 5-model扩展（614 violations coded, plan_010 completed）。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_violations_coded: 614\n    types_unanimous_dominant_fm: 3/6\n    types_majority_dominant_fm: 6/6\n    inter_coder_kappa: 0.517\n    percent_agreement: 0.656\n    disambiguation_awareness_overall: 0.046\n    disambiguation_awareness_claude: 0.11\n    disambiguation_awareness_others: <0.05\n    surface_adoption_rate: 0.88\n    escalate_to_user_rate: <0.01\n    cross_model_dominant_fm_agreement: 4/6 types\n    auth_scope_dominant_fm: unauthorized_escalation (majority)\n    incompleteness_dominant_fm: assumption_based_action (majority)\n    scopal_dominant_fm: scope_misapplication (majority)\n    auth_scope_escalation_rate: 0.692\n    auth_scope_restriction_rate: 0.0\n  result_rationale: 'Median档下C5的核心挑战是inter-coder κ=0.517（moderate）， 与actual completed\n    data完全一致。这意味着fine-grained per-type failure mode百分比不够可靠，paper中必须改用qualitative descriptors\n    （majority/plurality/co-dominant）而非精确百分比。但三个关键finding 不受κ问题影响：(1) Ambiguity Blindness\n    awareness=4.6%（binary判断， 不依赖fine-grained coding），(2) layer mechanism分化 （spec→guess-and-act\n    vs ling→misparse，dominant mode level一致6/6）， (3) auth_scope directional bias（69.2%\n    escalation, 0% restriction, binomial p=5.5e-5）。Claude的awareness=11%远高于其他模型（<5%），\n    与其低violation rate一致——safety training不只是拒绝,而是部分 meta-cognitive awareness。一位reviewer会要求C3的within-judge\n    fragility + error analysis的moderate κ combined导致C5降为 ''exploratory qualitative\n    analysis''而非validated taxonomy。 Rebuttal承诺camera-ready扩展human annotation。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Failure Mode Summary (Median Tier Qualitative Presentation)\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - dominant_mode\n    - qualifier\n    - layer_mechanism\n    - awareness_pct\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - unauthorized_escalation\n      - majority (69%)\n      - spec -> escalation\n      - 3.2\n    - - incompleteness\n      - assumption_based_action\n      - majority\n      - spec -> guess\n      - 4.8\n    - - scopal\n      - scope_misapplication\n      - majority\n      - ling -> misparse\n      - 5.1\n    - - lexical\n      - assumption_based_action\n      - plurality\n      - ling -> guess (surprising)\n      - 6.8\n    - - cond_prec\n      - scope_misappl + arb_rule\n      - co-dominant\n      - spec -> mixed\n      - 11.2\n    - - coreferential\n      - no dominant\n      - flat distribution\n      - ling -> diverse\n      - 8.5\n  - name: Ambiguity Blindness (Robust Metric)\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    - ci_95\n    - robust_to_kappa\n    rows:\n    - - awareness_rate\n      - 4.6%\n      - '[2.8%, 6.4%]'\n      - 'yes'\n    - - surface_adoption\n      - 88%\n      - '[85%, 91%]'\n      - 'yes'\n    - - escalate_to_user\n      - <1%\n      - '[0%, 1.5%]'\n      - 'yes'\n    - - conservative_refusal (coref)\n      - 6-11%\n      - '[4%, 14%]'\n      - 'yes'\n  - name: Auth Scope Directionality (plan_015)\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - escalation_rate\n      - 69.2%\n      - strong permissiveness bias\n    - - restriction_rate\n      - 0%\n      - never over-restricts\n    - - binomial_p\n      - '5.5e-5'\n      - highly significant directional bias\n    - - models_majority_escalation\n      - 4/5\n      - cross-model consistent\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 5: Failure mode x type stacked bar with qualitative labels (no precise\n    % in text)'\n  - 'Figure 6: Ambiguity Blindness — awareness vs surface adoption across types'\n  - Auth scope escalation vs restriction direction plot\n  analysis: 'C5在median档从独立contribution降为supporting analysis（§6）。 Ambiguity Blindness是最robust\n    finding。Inter-coder κ=0.517诚实披露， failure mode patterns presented at qualitative\n    level。 Auth_scope directionality（100% permissive, 0% restrictive） 是strong supplementary\n    finding supporting C4 interaction story。\n\n    '\n- name: reliability_test\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: '30 clauses × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 2 models = 360 episodes。\n    ICC per-clause violation rate reproducibility。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 360\n    overall_icc: 0.919\n    overall_icc_ci:\n    - 0.892\n    - 0.94\n    gpt54_icc: 0.921\n    gpt41_icc: 0.918\n    binary_icc: 0.847\n    per_type_icc_min: 0.807\n    per_type_icc_min_type: incompleteness\n    per_type_icc_max: 0.989\n    per_type_icc_max_type: scopal\n    ling_layer_avg_icc: 0.949\n    spec_layer_avg_icc: 0.835\n  result_rationale: 'Reliability test结果与actual completed data一致（ICC=0.919 [0.892,\n    0.940]）。 Median档下这是unambiguously positive的结果——per-clause violation rates 高度可复现，API\n    sampling noise不是concern。关键pattern： ling-layer ICC consistently higher than spec-layer（avg\n    0.949 vs 0.835）， 与disambiguation channel framework convergent——linguistic ambiguity\n    有更稳定的resolution pattern（agent倾向于同样的misparse）， spec-layer agents guess differently\n    each run。 Incompleteness ICC最低（0.807, still ''good''）因missing information 的interpretation\n    space最大。这个reliability-validity分离 （high ICC但plan_009揭示moderate judge accuracy）在median档下\n    成为一个nuance point：consistent measurement ≠ accurate measurement。 Paper中§4.5报告ICC作为reliability\n    evidence，同时在§4.6 judge calibration中区分reliability vs validity。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: ICC Summary\n    columns:\n    - grouping\n    - icc\n    - ci_lower\n    - ci_upper\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - overall\n      - 0.919\n      - 0.892\n      - 0.94\n      - excellent\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 0.921\n      - 0.874\n      - 0.943\n      - excellent\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 0.918\n      - 0.856\n      - 0.929\n      - excellent\n    - - binary\n      - 0.847\n      - 0.789\n      - 0.878\n      - good\n  - name: Per-type ICC (Layer Pattern)\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - layer\n    - icc\n    - ci_95\n    rows:\n    - - scopal\n      - ling\n      - 0.989\n      - '[0.968, 0.994]'\n    - - lexical\n      - ling\n      - 0.981\n      - '[0.948, 0.987]'\n    - - coreferential\n      - ling\n      - 0.976\n      - '[0.941, 0.984]'\n    - - auth_scope\n      - spec\n      - 0.857\n      - '[0.793, 0.896]'\n    - - cond_prec\n      - spec\n      - 0.856\n      - '[0.783, 0.890]'\n    - - incompleteness\n      - spec\n      - 0.807\n      - '[0.728, 0.851]'\n  figures_description:\n  - ICC forest plot per type, color-coded by layer, showing ling > spec pattern as\n    DCF convergent evidence\n  analysis: 'Reliability excellent且ling>spec pattern支持DCF。在median档下 这个结果不受任何threat——即使SOPBench部分复制、C3\n    fragile， τ²-bench内部的measurement reliability是solid的。\n\n    '\n- name: realism_validation\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: '合成ambiguity注入的生态效度验证。 与DRIP-R natural ambiguities的linguistic property比较。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_synthetic: 300\n    n_drip_r_natural: 87\n    flesch_kincaid_synthetic: 12.4\n    flesch_kincaid_drip_r: 11.8\n    fk_ks_p: 0.31\n    sentence_length_synthetic: 24.7\n    sentence_length_drip_r: 22.1\n    sl_ks_p: 0.08\n    ttr_synthetic: 0.72\n    ttr_drip_r: 0.69\n    ttr_ks_p: 0.15\n    parse_depth_synthetic: 5.8\n    parse_depth_drip_r: 5.2\n    pd_ks_p: 0.04\n    overall_distributional_overlap: 3/4 metrics non-significant KS\n  result_rationale: 'Realism validation在median档下结果mixed but adequate。 3/4 linguistic\n    metrics无显著分布差异（KS p>0.05）， 但parse_depth显著不同（p=0.04）——synthetic clauses更complex\n    （5.8 vs 5.2），因clause generation中为disambiguation control 添加了subordinate clauses。这在median档下不是致命问题但会被\n    一位reviewer提及——paper中报告为''comparable linguistic properties with slightly higher\n    parse complexity reflecting controlled design''。 DRIP-R data仅87条publicly available，样本量小但sufficient。\n    在median档下这个结果与SOPBench互补——SOPBench用不同benchmark 的real SOPs作为base，提供additional ecological\n    validity evidence （不同于synthetic on τ²-bench）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Linguistic Property Comparison\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - synthetic_mean\n    - drip_r_mean\n    - ks_stat\n    - ks_p\n    - sig\n    rows:\n    - - flesch_kincaid\n      - 12.4\n      - 11.8\n      - 0.098\n      - 0.31\n      - n.s.\n    - - sentence_length\n      - 24.7\n      - 22.1\n      - 0.142\n      - 0.08\n      - n.s.\n    - - type_token_ratio\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.69\n      - 0.112\n      - 0.15\n      - n.s.\n    - - parse_depth\n      - 5.8\n      - 5.2\n      - 0.167\n      - 0.04\n      - '*'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Overlapping violin plots: synthetic vs DRIP-R for 4 metrics, parse_depth showing\n    rightward shift'\n  analysis: '生态效度adequate。Parse depth差异在limitations披露。 SOPBench的real-SOP base clauses提供complementary\n    ecological evidence。\n\n    '\n- name: judge_calibration\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: 'LLM-as-judge calibration against human ground truth。 100 episodes\n    stratified，2 human annotators，precision/recall/F1。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_episodes: 100\n    human_inter_annotator_kappa_weighted: 0.762\n    cross_judge_kappa_weighted: 0.685\n    cross_judge_exact_agreement: 0.76\n    cross_judge_binary_kappa: 0.74\n    human_llm_pooled_kappa_weighted: 0.807\n    judge_human_binary_f1: 0.82\n    severity_tier_weighted_kappa: 0.72\n    auth_scope_binary_agreement: 0.78\n    incompleteness_binary_agreement: 0.85\n  result_rationale: 'Judge calibration actual data: human-LLM pooled κ_w=0.807, human\n    inter-annotator κ_w=0.762, cross-judge κ_w=0.685。 在median档下这些数字有两面性：(1) 好的一面——human-LLM\n    agreement (κ=0.807) 实际上HIGHER than human-human agreement (κ=0.762)， 这意味着LLM judge与human\n    ground truth的一致性优于humans之间， 这是strong validation evidence。(2) 一位reviewer的concern——\n    cross-judge κ=0.685只是''substantial''，且human inter-annotator κ=0.762低于ideal的0.80，说明task本身有inherent\n    subjectivity。 Median档的handling：paper在Method §4.4诚实报告所有κ values， highlight human-LLM\n    > human-human作为calibration validation， 但承认severity tier boundary（特别是tier1/tier2）存在subjectivity。\n    这个结果不需要correction（不同于previous dream中假设的systematic bias）， 因为actual data显示LLM judge\n    performs COMPARABLY to human experts。 但一位reviewer可能argue κ=0.762 human agreement本身偏低，\n    要求扩大sample size for camera-ready。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Judge Calibration Summary\n    columns:\n    - comparison\n    - kappa_weighted\n    - exact_agreement\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - human-LLM pooled\n      - 0.807\n      - N/A\n      - excellent — LLM matches human ground truth\n    - - human inter-annotator\n      - 0.762\n      - N/A\n      - substantial — task has inherent subjectivity\n    - - cross-judge (LLM-LLM)\n      - 0.685\n      - 0.76\n      - substantial — two LLM judges moderately agree\n    - - cross-judge binary\n      - 0.74\n      - N/A\n      - substantial\n  - name: Per-Type Judge Reliability Context\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - expected_judge_reliability\n    - note\n    rows:\n    - - incompleteness\n      - high\n      - clear missing-info violations easy to judge\n    - - cond_prec\n      - high\n      - explicit conflict violations clear-cut\n    - - auth_scope\n      - moderate\n      - boundary-exceeding vs reasonable-interpretation subjective\n    - - scopal\n      - moderate\n      - scope misapplication sometimes subtle\n    - - lexical\n      - moderate\n      - word-meaning violations depend on context\n    - - coreferential\n      - lower\n      - referential violations often partial/ambiguous themselves\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Agreement matrix: human1 vs human2 vs LLM-judge1 vs LLM-judge2 pairwise κ values'\n  - Per-severity-tier agreement rates showing tier boundary subjectivity\n  analysis: 'Judge calibration validates measurement chain。Human-LLM κ=0.807 > human-human\n    κ=0.762 是strong evidence。Median档下一位reviewer可能质疑sample size (n=100) 和human κ=0.762偏低，要求camera-ready\n    expansion。但不需要systematic correction—— 这是比previous dream更favorable的结果。\n\n    '\n- name: perturbation_control\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 'Non-ambiguity perturbation control。30 clause pairs × 2 conditions\n    × models。 Extended to 300 episodes (plan_014)。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 300\n    delta_perturb_pp: -0.67\n    ci_95_bootstrap:\n    - -8.0\n    - 6.67\n    ci_upper_bound: 6.67\n    ci_width: 14.67\n    mcnemar_p: 1.0\n    verdict: PASS\n    delta_ambiguity_pp: 34.0\n    delta_net_pp: 34.67\n    ratio: 0.0\n  result_rationale: 'Perturbation control actual data: Δ_perturb=-0.67pp (CI contains\n    0), verdict=PASS。这是所有档位下最unambiguous的positive result—— non-ambiguity perturbations造成essentially\n    zero effect (ratio≈0), 而ambiguity造成+34pp。Net effect 34.67pp远超任何threshold。 Median档下这个结果是C1\n    causal claim的backbone： 即使SOPBench replication弱化了cross-domain generalizability，\n    perturbation control确认τ²-bench内的ambiguity-specific causation 是clean的。CI width=14.67pp稍大（target\n    <10pp），但CI upper=6.67pp 远低于ambiguity effect，verdict清晰。一位reviewer可能注意到 CI width并建议further\n    expansion，但不会reject on this basis。 This result also transfers to SOPBench narrative——\n    如果SOPBench delta smaller，不是因为ambiguity isn''t causal， 而是因为rule-based verifier更strict或domain有moderating\n    effect。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Perturbation Control Verdict\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    - threshold\n    - verdict\n    rows:\n    - - delta_perturb\n      - -0.67pp\n      - <5pp\n      - PASS\n    - - CI_upper\n      - 6.67pp\n      - <10pp\n      - PASS\n    - - ratio\n      - ~0\n      - <0.15\n      - PASS\n    - - delta_net\n      - 34.67pp\n      - '>20pp'\n      - PASS\n    - - mcnemar_p\n      - '1.0'\n      - '>0.05'\n      - non-significant (good)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Three-bar comparison: delta_perturb (-0.67pp) vs delta_ambiguity (34pp) vs delta_net\n    (34.67pp) with CI'\n  analysis: 'Perturbation control是论文最强methodological evidence。 CI含0、ratio≈0、verdict=PASS。C1\n    causal claim安全。 SOPBench weaker replication不undermine causation——only generalizability。\n\n    '\n- name: sopbench_cross_benchmark\n  plan_id: plan_017\n  description: 'Cross-benchmark C1 replication on SOPBench (Li et al., 2025)。 Healthcare\n    + Bank domains, 100 clause pairs × 5 models = 1,000 episodes。 Rule-based verifier。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_clause_pairs: 100\n    healthcare_pairs: 50\n    bank_pairs: 50\n    types_covered:\n    - incompleteness\n    - auth_scope\n    - lexical\n    - conditional_precedence\n    total_episodes: 1000\n    episodes_valid: 982\n    episodes_failed: 18\n    failure_rate: 0.018\n    overall_amb_violation_rate: 0.295\n    overall_unamb_violation_rate: 0.112\n    overall_delta_pp: 18.3\n    overall_or: 3.31\n    overall_or_ci:\n    - 2.22\n    - 4.93\n    overall_p_value: <0.0001\n    c1_replicates: true\n    c1_effect_weaker: true\n    healthcare_delta_pp: 16.2\n    healthcare_amb_rate: 0.268\n    healthcare_unamb_rate: 0.106\n    bank_delta_pp: 20.4\n    bank_amb_rate: 0.322\n    bank_unamb_rate: 0.118\n    per_model_deltas:\n      gpt54_delta_pp: 22.5\n      gpt41_delta_pp: 19.8\n      claude_delta_pp: 12.1\n      qwen3_delta_pp: 18.4\n      deepseek_delta_pp: 18.7\n    per_type_sopbench:\n      incompleteness_rate: 0.392\n      auth_scope_rate: 0.215\n      lexical_rate: 0.338\n      cond_prec_rate: 0.235\n    sopbench_type_ranking:\n    - incompleteness\n    - lexical\n    - cond_prec\n    - auth_scope\n    tau2_type_ranking_ref:\n    - incompleteness\n    - lexical\n    - auth_scope\n    - cond_prec\n    type_rank_rho: 0.4\n    type_rank_p: 0.6\n    incompleteness_still_top: true\n    auth_scope_rank_drop: 'from #3 to #4'\n    cross_benchmark_effect_correlation: 0.58\n    rule_based_verifier_stricter: true\n    unamb_baseline_higher: true\n  result_rationale: 'SOPBench部分复制是median档的defining characteristic。 C1 binary effect显著复制（Δ=18.3pp,\n    OR=3.31, p<0.0001）， 但effect size大幅弱于τ²-bench的34pp。三个原因解释这个gap： (1) Rule-based\n    verifier更严格——SOPBench用deterministic rule matching 而非LLM judge。τ²-bench的LLM judge有~5-8pp\n    over-classification bias （plan_009显示human-LLM κ=0.807但not perfect），而rule-based\n    verifier 不会over-classify，因此SOPBench的raw numbers更conservative。 这意味着τ²-bench的true\n    effect可能closer to ~28pp（corrected）， 与SOPBench的18pp gap缩小到~10pp。 (2) Healthcare\n    domain的strict protocol culture——医疗SOPs本身 更structured，agents对healthcare policies更cautious（可能因training\n    data中medical scenarios的安全训练更intense），导致amb rate较低。 Healthcare delta仅16.2pp vs\n    Bank 20.4pp。 (3) Unambiguous baseline higher in SOPBench（11.2% vs τ²-bench 6.9%），\n    因为SOPBench的rule-based verifier对非ambiguity-related错误也更 敏感，压缩了delta space。 Type\n    ranking部分对齐（ρ=0.40, p=0.60, non-significant但方向正确）： incompleteness仍是#1（39.2%），确认其universally\n    dangerous地位。 但auth_scope从τ²-bench的#3降至SOPBench的#4（21.5%）， 因为healthcare/banking\n    domains的authorization boundaries更explicit （medical roles和banking permissions在SOPs中定义更清晰），\n    减少了agents escalation的空间。Lexical在bank domain上升 （banking术语歧义如\"account\"、\"interest\"比customer\n    service更prevalent）， 从#2维持。Cross-benchmark effect correlation=0.58（moderate）， 表明per-type\n    effect sizes across benchmarks有meaningful但不完美的对应关系。 18个failed episodes主要因SOPBench环境setup不perfect\n    （healthcare domain的complex multi-step procedures偶发parse errors）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: SOPBench C1 Replication Summary\n    columns:\n    - benchmark\n    - domain\n    - n_episodes\n    - amb_rate\n    - unamb_rate\n    - delta_pp\n    - OR\n    - p_value\n    rows:\n    - - tau2-bench\n      - retail+airline\n      - 2997\n      - 0.41\n      - 0.069\n      - 34.0\n      - 15.1\n      - <0.0001\n    - - SOPBench\n      - healthcare+bank\n      - 982\n      - 0.295\n      - 0.112\n      - 18.3\n      - 3.31\n      - <0.0001\n    - - SOPBench\n      - healthcare\n      - 487\n      - 0.268\n      - 0.106\n      - 16.2\n      - 3.06\n      - <0.001\n    - - SOPBench\n      - bank\n      - 495\n      - 0.322\n      - 0.118\n      - 20.4\n      - 3.58\n      - <0.0001\n  - name: SOPBench Per-Model Results\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - amb_rate\n    - unamb_rate\n    - delta_pp\n    - p_value\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 0.34\n      - 0.115\n      - 22.5\n      - <0.001\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.122\n      - 19.8\n      - <0.001\n    - - qwen3-235b\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.116\n      - 18.4\n      - <0.005\n    - - deepseek-v3\n      - 0.31\n      - 0.123\n      - 18.7\n      - <0.005\n    - - claude\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.099\n      - 12.1\n      - <0.05\n  - name: Type Ranking Comparison (Ambiguous Only)\n    columns:\n    - rank\n    - tau2_bench_type\n    - tau2_rate\n    - sopbench_type\n    - sopbench_rate\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - incompleteness\n      - 53.6%\n      - incompleteness\n      - 39.2%\n    - - 2\n      - lexical\n      - 42.8%\n      - lexical\n      - 33.8%\n    - - 3\n      - auth_scope\n      - 41.6%\n      - cond_prec\n      - 23.5%\n    - - 4\n      - scopal\n      - 39.4%\n      - auth_scope\n      - 21.5%\n    - - 5\n      - cond_prec\n      - 36.8%\n      - N/A (not tested)\n      - N/A\n    - - 6\n      - coreferential\n      - 31.6%\n      - N/A (not tested)\n      - N/A\n  - name: Cross-Benchmark Summary Metrics\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    - median_tier_range\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - sopbench_c1_delta_pp\n      - 18.3\n      - '[15, 25]'\n      - within range, significant\n    - - sopbench_type_rank_rho\n      - 0.4\n      - '[0.3, 0.7]'\n      - partial alignment\n    - - sopbench_incomp_rate\n      - 39.2%\n      - '[35%, 55%]'\n      - still highest type\n    - - cross_benchmark_r\n      - 0.58\n      - '[0.4, 0.75]'\n      - moderate correlation\n    - - sopbench_OR\n      - 3.31\n      - <5 (median tier)\n      - significant but weaker\n  - name: Effect Size Gap Decomposition\n    columns:\n    - factor\n    - estimated_contribution_pp\n    - evidence\n    rows:\n    - - rule-based vs LLM judge strictness\n      - ~6-8pp\n      - LLM judge over-classification from plan_009\n    - - domain moderation (healthcare caution)\n      - ~4-5pp\n      - healthcare 16.2pp vs bank 20.4pp\n    - - higher unambiguous baseline\n      - ~3-4pp\n      - 11.2% vs 6.9% compresses delta\n    - - residual (true domain effect)\n      - ~2-3pp\n      - genuine domain-dependence\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired forest plot: tau2-bench vs SOPBench per-type delta_pp with 95% CI, showing\n    parallel but attenuated pattern'\n  - 'Cross-benchmark effect correlation scatter: per-type (tau2-bench delta vs SOPBench\n    delta), r=0.58'\n  - 'Domain comparison: healthcare vs bank delta_pp per model, showing healthcare\n    consistently lower'\n  analysis: 'SOPBench部分复制是median档的核心结果。Binary effect跨domain confirmed （p<0.0001），但effect\n    size因benchmark strictness和domain moderation 大幅减弱（18.3pp vs 34pp）。Incompleteness\n    universally #1（39.2%）， auth_scope在structured domains排序下降。Paper main text一句话： ''Partial\n    cross-benchmark replication on SOPBench (Healthcare+Banking) confirms the binary\n    ambiguity effect (Δ=18.3pp, p<0.0001) while revealing domain-dependent type severity\n    ordering (ρ=0.40).'' Appendix详细报告。 C1 claim加caveat: ''effect size varies by benchmark\n    strictness (OR=15.1 LLM-judged vs OR=3.3 rule-based) and domain (healthcare Δ=16.2pp\n    < banking Δ=20.4pp < customer-service Δ=34.0pp)''。 C2 hierarchy从''universal 3-tier''降为''robust\n    in customer-service, partially replicated — incompleteness universally dangerous,\n    mid-tier ordering domain-sensitive''。 plan_013的7/7 C1 replication（含Gemini/LLaMA）补偿SOPBench弱复制，\n    形成''model-universal but domain-moderated''的balanced narrative。\n\n    '\n- name: classifier_poc\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'Binary ambiguity detector PoC。 DeBERTa-v3-large fine-tuned on clause\n    pairs (original plan)。 Supplemented by LLM-based classification (plan_012 completed)。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    deberta_binary_f1: 0.79\n    deberta_binary_precision: 0.82\n    deberta_binary_recall: 0.76\n    deberta_binary_fpr: 0.048\n    deberta_macro_f1_6type: 0.55\n    llm_binary_f1: 0.806\n    llm_macro_f1_6type: 0.632\n    llm_best_type_f1:\n      conditional_precedence: 0.94\n    llm_worst_type_f1:\n      incompleteness: 0.34\n    training_time_hours: 6\n    gpu_used: 1x A100\n  result_rationale: 'Median档下classifier PoC有两个版本的结果： (1) DeBERTa fine-tuned: binary\n    F1=0.79（adequate for PoC）， 6-type macro F1=0.55（weak）。Type-level极不均匀： CP F1=0.91（structural\n    signal强），incompleteness F1=0.31 （absence无positive signal）。与Chantree 2006一致—— structural\n    ambiguity比semantic ambiguity更可检测。 (2) LLM-based (plan_012 completed): binary F1=0.806,\n    6-type macro F1=0.632。LLM优于DeBERTa因为可以leverage semantic understanding，但incompleteness仍最差（F1=0.34）。\n    在median档下classifier是appendix material，不作为独立contribution。 Binary detection viable（F1~0.80），type\n    classification需要 更大训练数据或更sophisticated approach。一位reviewer可能suggest 这是separate\n    future work——rebuttal同意并scope down to appendix。 DeBERTa vs LLM comparison本身有minor\n    interest （shows linguistic detector vs semantic detector trade-off） 但不值得在main\n    text花space。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Classifier Comparison (DeBERTa vs LLM)\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - binary_f1\n    - 6type_macro_f1\n    - best_type\n    - worst_type\n    rows:\n    - - DeBERTa-v3-large\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.55\n      - cond_prec (0.91)\n      - incompleteness (0.31)\n    - - GPT-4.1 few-shot\n      - 0.806\n      - 0.632\n      - cond_prec (0.94)\n      - incompleteness (0.34)\n  - name: Per-type F1 (LLM-based, plan_012 actual)\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - f1\n    - note\n    rows:\n    - - conditional_precedence\n      - 0.94\n      - structural conflict signal strong\n    - - scopal\n      - 0.75\n      - scope markers detectable\n    - - coreferential\n      - 0.7\n      - pronoun/RC patterns\n    - - authorization_scope\n      - 0.58\n      - boundary language moderate signal\n    - - lexical\n      - 0.39\n      - word-level, few surface cues\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 0.34\n      - absence has no positive signal\n  figures_description:\n  - Per-type F1 bar chart comparing DeBERTa vs LLM, both showing same difficulty gradient\n  analysis: Classifier是appendix。Binary detection viable (F1~0.80), type classification\n    poor for absence-based types (incompleteness). Practical contribution limited\n    but demonstrates feasibility。 不影响main paper score。\n","numLines":1274,"startLine":1,"totalLines":127