{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0193XpmcWvKRCGHEDvmb86xN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the paper and the review context carefully, then dispatch two reviewers for the full roundtable review process.\n\nThe paper is: \"Not All Policy Ambiguity Is Equal: Differential Vulnerability Profiles Across LLM Agent Families\"\n\nLet me first understand the paper's structure and claims:\n- C1: Binary effect of policy ambiguity (+34.0pp, OR=15.1)\n- C2: Three-tier type hierarchy (incompleteness > mid > coreferential)\n- C3: Layer effect (spec > ling, but fragile — moved to appendix)\n- C4: Model × type interaction (auth_scope 52pp range)\n\n\n- C5: Error analysis showing ambiguity blindness at under 5% awareness, with SOPBench replication showing an 18.3pp effect and perturbation controls at -0.67pp\n\nNow I'm setting up the reviewer dispatch with R1 handling methods and experiments while R2 focuses on novelty and related work positioning, then running through the full roundtable sequence: independent assessments, cross-reviewer sharing, convergence on key issues, and final synthesis.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":37094,"cache_read_input_tokens":24303,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":37094},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f8afb83-87c5-4ef3-9a6a-2fa2980a14de","uuid":"5a0623af-b04c-4cd0-a381-0dd08faa3db7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0193XpmcWvKRCGHEDvmb86xN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dispatching two independent reviewers (R1: Methods+Experiments, R2: Novelty+Related Work) in parallel."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":37094,"cache_read_input_tokens":24303,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":37094},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f8afb83-87c5-4ef3-9a6a-2fa2980a14de","uuid":"9876add1-b52b-4866-aa88-556ba7fc6999"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0193XpmcWvKRCGHEDvmb86xN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XWzwncAZYV2VZk5yjFA1X1","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for an EMNLP 2026 ARR submission. Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Not All Policy Ambiguity Is Equal: Differential Vulnerability Profiles Across LLM Agent Families\"\n\nThe paper introduces a matched-pair causal design over a six-type, two-layer ambiguity taxonomy, evaluating 2,997 agent episodes across 5 models (GPT-5.4, GPT-4.1, Claude Sonnet 4.6, Qwen3-235B, DeepSeek-v3) on τ²-bench. Key claims:\n- C1: Ambiguous policy clauses increase safety-violation rates by +34.0pp (OR=15.1, p<0.0001)\n- C2: Three-tier type hierarchy (incompleteness 53.6% > mid cluster 36.8-42.8% > coreferential 31.6%)\n- C4: Model×type interaction with 52pp range for authorization scope\n- C3 (appendix, exploratory): Spec-layer > ling-layer (Δ=6.08pp, p=0.017 but fragile within-judge)\n- Error analysis: Ambiguity Blindness (<5% meta-cognitive awareness, >88% surface adoption, <1% escalation)\n- SOPBench cross-benchmark replication: binary effect confirmed (Δ=18.3pp, OR=3.31) but weaker\n- Perturbation control: Δ=-0.67pp (near zero), isolating ambiguity-specific causation\n\n## Paper Details\n\n**Section 3 - Taxonomy**: Two-layer (specification: incompleteness, auth_scope, cond_prec; linguistic: lexical, scopal, coreferential). Grounded in Li et al. and Massey et al.\n\n**Section 4 - Experimental Design**:\n- 300 matched clause pairs (50/type × 6 types), amb vs unamb variants\n- Spec-layer needs more tokens to disambiguate (34.0 vs 14.8 tokens, p<0.001)\n- Mini-pilot: 20 episodes validating coreferential and auth_scope\n- 5 models × 300 clauses × 2 conditions = 3,000 target, 2,981 valid (99.4%)\n- Cross-judge evaluation: each model judged by different model\n- Reliability test: ICC=0.919 [0.892, 0.940], ling-layer ICC higher (0.949 vs 0.835)\n- Judge calibration: human-LLM κ_w=0.807 > human-human κ_w=0.762; cross-judge κ_w=0.685; binary F1=0.82\n- Realism validation: 3/4 KS tests n.s. vs DRIP-R; parse depth sig (p=0.04)\n\n**Section 5 - Results**:\n- C1: Pooled +34.0pp, OR=15.1, all 5 models p<1e-14. Logistic regression: condition β=2.278, z=19.65; token_delta β=0.022, z=3.49\n- Perturbation control: Δ=-0.67pp, CI [-8.0, 6.67], McNemar p=1.0\n- C2: χ²=28.02, p=3.6e-5, V=0.137, power=0.993. TOST: ±15pp 7/15 non-equiv; ±10pp 11/15; ±5pp 14/15\n- C4: Model main χ²=31.02, p=3.0e-6, V=0.102. Auth_scope range 52pp (Claude 12% to GPT-5.4 64%). Auth_scope directionality: 69.2% escalation, 0% restriction, binomial p=5.5e-5\n- SOPBench replication: Δ=18.3pp, OR=3.31. Healthcare Δ=16.2pp, Bank Δ=20.4pp. Type rank ρ=0.40 (n.s.)\n\n**Section 6 - Error Analysis**: 614 violation traces, inter-coder κ=0.517 (moderate). Ambiguity awareness 4.6% [2.8, 6.4]. Dominant modes presented at majority/plurality level.\n\n**Appendices**: B - C3 layer effect (exploratory), C - classifier PoC (DeBERTa F1=0.79, LLM F1=0.806 binary), D - TOST analysis\n\n**Limitations**: Domain-limited (τ²-bench retail+airline, SOPBench healthcare+bank), synthetic clauses (slightly higher parse depth), C3 layer effect fragile\n\n## Review Context from experiment plan\n- Total episodes across τ²-bench and SOPBench: ~3,979\n- Classifier PoC is appendix material\n- C3 moved to appendix as exploratory\n- SOPBench results in appendix with main-text summary\n- Error analysis inter-coder κ=0.517 honestly disclosed\n- 7-model replication (including Gemini/LLaMA from plan_013) is mentioned in the experiment plan but NOT in the paper — only 5 models appear\n\n## Your Task\nProvide a detailed review focused on:\n1. **Soundness of experimental design** (matched-pair design, perturbation control, confound handling)\n2. **Statistical methodology** (test choices, effect sizes, multiple comparisons, power)\n3. **Measurement validity** (judge calibration, ICC, inter-coder reliability)\n4. **Reproducibility** (enough detail to replicate?)\n5. **Completeness** (missing experiments from the plan? Missing analyses?)\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Scoring (ARR Overall Assessment, half-point scale 1-5):\n- 5 = Award consideration (top 2.5%)\n- 4 = Conference accept\n- 3 = Findings accept\n- 2 = Resubmit next cycle\n- 1 = Do not resubmit\n\nAlso score: Soundness (1-5), Excitement (1-5), Reproducibility (1-5)\n\nAcceptance rate: ~21% for main, meaning a score of 4+ is needed for main conference.\n\nWrite your review in this format:\n```\n## R1 Review: Methods and Experiments\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\n[Numbered list]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Numbered list]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[Numbered list]\n\n### Missing from Experiment Plan\n[What experiments from the plan are missing in the paper?]\n\n### Minor Issues\n[Numbered list]\n\n### Scores\n- Soundness: X/5\n- Excitement: X/5  \n- Reproducibility: X/5\n- Overall: X.X/5\n- Confidence: X/5\n```\n\nBe rigorous and calibrated. A \"3\" is Findings-level, not a rejection. A \"4\" requires strong, well-executed work. Calibrate to EMNLP acceptance rate (~21% main).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":37094,"cache_read_input_tokens":24303,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":37094},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f8afb83-87c5-4ef3-9a6a-2fa2980a14de","uuid":"7570fc06-1b16-46b9-994e-b700265b263b"}
